## 4. Drift Detection: Supported Metrics and Thresholds

### 4.1 Platform-Native Drift Metrics (in `feature_observability.drift.*` namespace)

| Metric Namespace | Statistical Test | Feature Type | Decision Logic |
|-----------------|-----------------|--------------|----------------|
| `feature_observability.drift.ks_d` | Kolmogorov-Smirnov statistic | Continuous | `statistic > 0.2` → drifted |
| `feature_observability.drift.ks_pvalue` | KS p-value | Continuous | `p_value <= 0.05` → drifted |
| `feature_observability.drift.psi` | Population Stability Index | Continuous | `PSI > 0.2` → drifted |
| Chi-squared | Chi-squared test | Categorical | `p_value <= 0.05` → drifted |
| Hellinger Distance | Hellinger distance | All (binned) | Configurable threshold |

**Source**: [Feature Drift Detection Architecture Proposal](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/KYC/pages/6866709029), [Design: ML Lens Platform Data Drift Detection](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6738511349)

### 4.2 Custom/Team-Computed Drift Metrics (Emitted by teams, stored in ML Lens)

Teams compute their own metrics (e.g., Jensen-Shannon divergence, cosine similarity for embeddings, Wasserstein distance) in ML Studio jobs and emit to ML Lens as custom metrics.

**Relevant for NLP/embedding drift**: Cosine similarity is NOT a platform-native drift metric. It must be:
1. Computed by the team in a custom ML Studio module or batch job
2. Emitted via `send_metrics()` with an appropriate namespace (e.g., `ai_gateway.drift.cosine_similarity`)
3. Alerting configured on top of the emitted metric

The One Pager mentions "embedding drift" as a planned/future capability, but as of May 2026it is not yet platformized.

### 4.3 Auto-Selection Logic for Drift Tests

The platform auto-selects statistical test based on feature type:
- **Continuous numeric** (n_unique > 5): KS test (small data≤1000), Wasserstein/PSI (large data)
- **Categorical** (n_unique ≤ 5): Chi-squared test
- **Binary** (n_unique ≤ 2): Z-score proportion test

**Source**: [Feature Drift Detection Architecture Proposal](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/KYC/pages/6866709029), [POC on Evidently](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020b96ba8eb7c714ceb83be01da61de2c9f/pages/6495486867)

### 4.4 Reference Windows (Baseline Strategies)

| Strategy | Config | Use Case |
|----------|--------|----------|
| Sliding window | `reference_window: "28d"` (default) | Short-term operational drift |
| Fixed period | `start: "2024-01-01", end: "2024-01-07"` | Training distribution baseline |
| User-supplied stats | `baseline: { mean: X, stddev: Y }` | Known good state |

