## 5. ML Lens Dashboards and Visualization

### 5.1 UI Capabilities

The ML Lens UI (part of AI Platform portal) provides:
- **Time-series charts** for any metric in the store
- **Run-level comparison** (metrics across different ML Studio runs)
- **Tag-based filtering and slicing** (by tenant, region, model, feature_service)
- **Alert history and status** display
- **Feature health dashboards** (drift over time, freshness, volume)

### 5.2 Dashboard Categories

| Dashboard Type | What It Shows | How It's Powered |
|---------------|---------------|-----------------|
| **Feature Health** | Drift scores, null%, freshness per feature | `feature_observability.drift.*` metrics from StarRocks |
| **Training Metrics** | NDCG, loss, AUC per run/workflow | Team-emitted metrics via SDK |
| **Data Quality** | Null counts, statistics, profiling results | `ml_platform_data_profiling.*` namespace |
| **Workflow Operational** | Run duration, success rate, resource usage | Platform-emitted metrics |
| **Model Serving** | Latency, error rate, prediction distribution | Team/platform hybrid |

### 5.3 Access Points
- **ML Lens UI** (primary): Charts, alert management, metric exploration
- **ML Studio Portal**: Integrated views in Workflow/Blueprint/Run detail pages
- **Databricks**: Metrics from ML Lens are available for custom dashboards in Databricks via Socrates replication
- **Atlas ML CLI**: Bulk alert registration

**Source**: [ML Lens FY26 H1 Outcomes](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6178128251), [Search Plex ML Lens Observability](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~93171358/pages/6660205781)

