## 6. Alerting System (Notifications)

### 6.1 Alert Detection Modes

| Mode | Measure | Operator | Example |
|------|---------|----------|---------|
| **Standard deviation** | `std` | `>=` | `tolerance: 3` (3-sigma) |
| **Expected value** (threshold) | `expected_value` | `>=`, `<=`, `>`, `<` | `value: 0.85` |
| **No data** | `no_data` | `>=` | `value: 86400` (seconds) |
| **Complex (N-of-M)** | group logic | `AND`/`OR`/`N_OF` | 2-of-3 conditions |

### 6.2 Alert Routing

| Destination | Format |
|------------|--------|
| **Slack** | Channel or DM via `{"type": "slack", "values": [{"id": "#channel", "type": "channel"}]}` |
| **JSM Ops** | Team/User/Schedule/Escalation via `{"type": "jsm_ops", "values": [...]}` |
| **StreamHub** (event bus) | For downstream service consumption (e.g., auto-retraining triggers) |

### 6.3 Notification Payload

Alerts include: feature/score identifier, scope (tenant/product/region), comparison window, detected magnitude (KS p-value, z-score), last-seen time, runbook link.

**Source**: [ML Lens Notifications Infrastructure Design](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/5688298043), [ML Lens Alerting Requirements](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/5989280688)

