# SignalFx Detectors-as-Code & Per-Endpoint SLO IaC Encoding: Research Findings

## 1. Atlassian's SignalFx IaC Toolchain Architecture

### What it is
Atlassian uses a layered infrastructure-as-code stack to manage SignalFx operational artifacts (detectors, dashboards, charts) and TOME SLOs. The full toolchain consists of five interconnected components:

| Tool | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| **Terraform** | IaC language — defines detectors, charts, dashboards, and SLOs in `.tf` files |
| **SignalFx Terraform Provider** (`splunk-terraform/signalfx`) | Provider that translates Terraform resources into SignalFx API calls |
| **TOME Terraform Provider** | Provider for Atlassian's SLO tracking platform (go/tome) |
| **SignalFM (sfm)** | CLI wrapper over Terraform for local SignalFx automation — handles init, plan, apply, destroy |
| **Sauron** | Atlassian service that auto-deploys Terraform changes on commit to master via Bitbucket Pipelines |

### How it works — Deployment Flow
```
Developer authors .tf files → PR review → Merge to master → Sauron (via sauron-pipe in BB Pipelines) → terraform plan → terraform apply → SignalFx/TOME updated
```

On non-master branches, Sauron runs in `dry-run` mode (plan only, no apply), providing validation feedback on PRs.

### How it applies to skill/tool design
An AI employee authoring detectors would:
1. Generate Terraform HCL for `signalfx_detector` and `tome_slo` resources
2. Validate using `terraform fmt` + `terraform validate` + `sfm plan` (local testing)
3. Create a PR in the appropriate Bitbucket repo
4. After human approval and merge, Sauron auto-deploys

**Human confirmation required**: PR approval before merge (deploying detectors to production). The AI can autonomously generate HCL, validate syntax, and create PRs but should NOT auto-merge.

**Source**: [AI Best practice for TOME & SignalFX with Terraform](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~701218d2df3d0880048348a2a3ced7b9eb167/pages/6702725855), [Sauron 101](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~510798821/pages/1772291789)

---

## 2. `signalfx_detector` Resource — Complete Anatomy

### What it is
The core Terraform resource for defining alerting rules. Each detector monitors metrics via SignalFlow and fires alerts when conditions are met.

### How it works — Full Resource Schema

```hcl
resource "signalfx_detector" "<resource_name>" {
  # --- Header ---
  name              = "${var.resource_name_prefix}<Human-readable name>"
  description       = "<Description of what this detector monitors>"
  
  # --- Display ---
  show_data_markers = true
  show_event_lines= false
  time_range        = 86400  # UI chart view in seconds (1d)
  max_delay         = 900    # Max seconds to wait for late-arriving data
  
  # --- Ownership ---
  teams             = [var.signalfx_team_id]
  tags              = ["team-tag", "service-tag"]
  
  # --- SignalFlow Program ---
  program_text      = <<-EOT
    A = data('<metric_name>', filter=filter('<dimension>', '<value>') and filter('<dim2>', '<val2>'),
        rollup='sum',
        extrapolation='last_value'
    ).sum(by=['<grouping_dim>']).publish(label='A')
    detect(when(A > threshold(<value>), lasting='<duration>')).publish('<detect_label>')
  EOT

  # --- Alert Rules (one per detect().publish()) ---
  rule {
    detect_label          = "<detect_label>"  # MUST match detect().publish() exactly
    severity              = "Critical"  # Critical|Major|Minor|Warning|Info
    disabled              = false
    notifications         = ["Opsgenie,<cred_id>,<team_name>,<team_uuid>,Team"]
    parameterized_subject = "{{ruleSeverity}}: {{{detectorName}}}"
    parameterized_body    = <<-EOT
      {{#if anomalous}}
        🚨 Rule "{{{ruleName}}}" triggered at {{timestamp}}.
        Triggering condition: {{{readableRule}}}
        Signal value: {{inputs.A.value}}
      {{else}}
        ✅ Rule "{{{ruleName}}}" cleared at {{timestamp}}.
      {{/if}}
      {{#if runbookUrl}}📖 Runbook: {{{runbookUrl}}}{{/if}}
    EOT
    runbook_url           = "<URL to runbook>"
    tip                   = "<Quick troubleshooting tip>"
  }
}
```

### Key Attributes Enumerated

| Attribute | Type | Required | Description |
|-----------|------|----------|-------------|
| `name` | string | ✅ | Detector display name in UI |
| `description` | string | ❌ | Human-readable description |
| `program_text` | string | ✅ | SignalFlow program defining metrics and conditions |
| `teams` | list(string) | ❌ | SignalFx team IDs for ownership |
| `tags` | list(string) | ❌ | Searchable tags |
| `time_range` | number | ❌ | Default chart view (seconds) |
| `max_delay` | number | ❌ | Max seconds to wait for data |
| `show_data_markers` | bool | ❌ | Show markers on chart |
| `show_event_lines` | bool | ❌ | Show event lines on chart |

**Rule block attributes:**

| Attribute | Type | Required | Description |
|-----------|------|----------|-------------|
| `detect_label` | string | ✅ | Must match `detect().publish('<label>')` EXACTLY |
| `severity` | string | ✅ | Critical, Major, Minor, Warning, Info |
| `disabled` | bool | ❌ | Whether rule is active |
| `notifications` | list(string) | ❌ | Notification targets |
| `parameterized_subject` | string | ❌ | Alert subject (Handlebars) |
| `parameterized_body` | string | ❌ | Alert body (Handlebars) |
| `runbook_url` | string | ❌ | Link to runbook |
| `tip` | string | ❌ | Quick troubleshooting hint |

### Severity-to-OpsGenie Mapping
```
Critical → P1
Major    → P2
Minor    → P3
Warning  → P4
Info     → P5 (informational, no page)
```

### Notification Formats
```hcl
# OpsGenie
"Opsgenie,<credential_id>,<team_name>,<team_uuid>,Team"
# Slack
"Slack,DxJ_pZzA0N0,<channel_name_no_hash>"
# Team (SignalFx team notification)
"Team,<signalfx_team_id>"
```

**Atlassian credential IDs (not secret):**
- Slack: `DxJ_pZzA0N0`
- OpsGenie: `D2c_4qUA4AA`

### Handlebars Template Variables for Alert Messages
```
{{ruleName}}                - Rule name
{{detectorName}}             - Detector name
{{ruleSeverity}}             - Severity level
{{timestamp}}                - Alert trigger time
{{inputs.A.value}}           - Value of signal labeled'A'
{{dimensions.<name>}}        - Dimension value
{{{readableRule}}}           - Human-readable condition
{{{runbookUrl}}}             - Runbook URL
{{#if anomalous}}...{{/if}} - Alert vs clear conditional
{{#notEmpty dimensions}}...- If dimensions present
{{dateTimeFormat timestamp format="full"}} - Formatted timestamp
```

**Source**: [How To: Add New SignalFx Detectors in Terraform](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120204aa07fe7450f489899b60900ad6a0967/pages/5977304542), [How to migrate existing SignalFX Detectors to Terraform Code](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/3w/pages/5743289856), [RFO SignalFx detectors](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/cdr/pages/6876959168)

