## 9. Integration with OpsGenie (Alert Routing)

### What it is
SignalFx detectors route alerts to OpsGenie, which dispatches to on-call responders based on schedules.

### How it works
1. Create OpsGenie integration in OpsGenie (Settings → Integrations → SignalFx)
2. Note the API URL and configure in SignalFx
3. In Terraform, use notification string format: `"Opsgenie,<credential_id>,<team_name>,<team_uuid>,Team"`
4. Severity mapping is automatic: Critical→P1, Major→P2, Minor→P3, Warning→P4

### Integration for responsible-ai-api detectors
Per OPP-202605-04: "Route all to the team OpsGenie rotation."

```hcl
locals {
  opsgenie_notification = "Opsgenie,D2c_4qUA4AA,${var.opsgenie_team_name},${var.opsgenie_team_id},Team"
}
```

**Source**: [Integrate Opsgenie with SignalFx](https://support.atlassian.com/opsgenie/docs/integrate-opsgenie-with-signalfx/), [HOWTO: Create new SignalFX detectors/alerts with TerraForm](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020f40d1f1a782747b8ae1eb16415e6a594/pages/3313960184)

