## 4. Per-Endpoint SLO Encoding via TOME Terraform

### What it is
TOME is Atlassian's SLO tracking and monitoring platform. SLOs are defined in Terraform using the `tome_slo` resource and deployed via Sauron. The hierarchy is: **Team → Product → Capability → SLO**.

### How it works — Resource Structure

#### Capability (Groups SLOs)
```hcl
resource "tome_capability" "prompt_moderation" {
  name        = "Prompt Moderation"
  owner       = var.capability_owner  # Account ID
  product     = tome_product.responsible_ai.id
  team        = var.team
  importance  = "tier1"
  description = "Prompt moderation endpoint for responsible AI"
}
```

#### Reliability SLO (per-endpoint)
```hcl
resource "tome_slo" "prompt_moderation_reliability" {
  name        = "Prompt moderation outcomes are reliably processed"
  capability  = tome_capability.prompt_moderation.id
  service_id  = "responsible-ai-api"
  type        = "RELIABILITY"
  is_draft    = false
  objective   = 99.9
  description = "5xx rate ≤ 0.1% for /v1/moderation/prompt"runbook_url = "https://..."
  good_query =<<-EOT
    A = data('http.server.requests.hg.histogram', 
        filter=filter('le', '+Inf')
            and filter('micros_service_id', 'responsible-ai-api') 
            and filter('uri', '/v1/moderation/prompt') 
            and filter('status', '2*'),
        rollup='sum').sum().fill(0).publish(label='A', enable=True)
  EOT
  
  bad_query = <<-EOT
    B = data('http.server.requests.hg.histogram', 
        filter=filter('le', '+Inf') 
            and filter('micros_service_id', 'responsible-ai-api') 
            and filter('uri', '/v1/moderation/prompt') 
            and filter('status', '5*'),
        rollup='sum').sum().fill(0).publish(label='B', enable=True)
  EOT
}
```

#### Performance SLO (Latency, per-endpoint)
```hcl
resource "tome_slo" "prompt_moderation_performance" {
  name        = "Prompt moderation outcomes are processed within 6000 milliseconds"
  capability  = tome_capability.prompt_moderation.id
  service_id  = "responsible-ai-api"
  type        = "PERFORMANCE"
  is_draft    = false
  objective   = 99
  description = "P99 ≤ 6s for /v1/moderation/prompt"
  
  good_query = <<-EOT
    A = data('http.server.requests.hg.histogram', 
        filter=filter('le', '6000') 
            and filter('micros_service_id', 'responsible-ai-api') 
            and filter('uri', '/v1/moderation/prompt') 
            and filter('status', '2*'),
        rollup='sum').sum().fill(0).publish(label='A', enable=True)
  EOT
  
  bad_query = <<-EOT
    B = data('http.server.requests.hg.histogram', 
        filter=filter('le', '6000') 
            and filter('micros_service_id', 'responsible-ai-api') 
            and filter('uri', '/v1/moderation/prompt') 
            and filter('status', '2*'),
        rollup='sum').sum().fill(0).publish(label='B', enable=False)
    C = data('http.server.requests.hg.histogram', 
        filter=filter('le', '+Inf') 
            and filter('micros_service_id', 'responsible-ai-api') 
            and filter('uri', '/v1/moderation/prompt') 
            and filter('status', '2*'),
        rollup='sum').sum().fill(0).publish(label='C', enable=False)
    D = (C-B).above(0, clamp=True).fill(0).publish(label='D', enable=True)
  EOT
}
```

#### SLO Group (Service Archetype pattern, newer)
```hcl
resource "tome_slo_group" "moderation_reliability" {
  name               = "Moderation Endpoint Reliability"
  capability         = tome_capability.prompt_moderation.id
  service_id         = "responsible-ai-api"
  slo_group_type     = "SERVICE_ARCHETYPE"
  type               = "RELIABILITY"
  is_draft           = false
  objective          = 99.9
  auto_sync          = true
  enabled_alerts     = "GRADUAL,MODERATE,STEEP,ULTRA_STEEP"
  
  good_query_template = <<-EOT
    A = data('http.server.requests.count', 
        filter=$${filter} and filter('status', '2*'),
        rollup='sum').sum().fill(0).publish(label='A', enable=True)
  EOT
  
  bad_query_template = <<-EOT
    B = data('http.server.requests.count', 
        filter=$${filter} and filter('status', '5*'),
        rollup='sum').sum().fill(0).publish(label='B', enable=True)
  EOT
  
  manual_tags = {
    env= "prod"
    cloud_sla_critical_path= "yes"
    cloud_sla_covered_experience = "AI Moderation"
  }
}
```

### TOME Alert Burn Rate Types
When `enabled_alerts` is configured, TOME fires alerts into OpsGenie based on error budget burn rates:
- **GRADUAL** — slow, sustained burn over hours (P4)
- **MODERATE** — moderate burn rate (P3)
- **STEEP** — rapid burn needing prompt attention (P2)
- **ULTRA_STEEP** — critical burn rate (P1)

### The Specific AI Gateway / responsible-ai-api Context

From **[STRA-202605-07]** (Jira issue AI-256), the proposed per-endpoint SLOs for the responsible-ai-api are:
- `prompt` P99 ≤ 6s
- `agent` P99 ≤ 8s
- `image` P99 ≤ 10s
- `output` first-token ≤ 2s
- 5xx rate ≤ 0.1%
- fail-open rate ≤ 0.5%

From **[STRA-202605-06]** (Jira issue on Tony's recent activity), these SLOs need to be encoded in IaC under `operations/terraform/`.

Current state (from AI-264 grep): `grep -c "signalfx_detector" operations/terraform/*.tf == 0` — zero detectors in IaC today.

**Source**: [Smart Experiences TOME SLO checklist](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SMRT/pages/1534861484), [Service Archetype SLO Groups in Tome](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/OBSERVABILITY/blog/2026/02/25/6499617674), [STRA-202605-07](https://hello.jira.atlassian.cloud/browse/AI-256)

