## 6. Repository Structure & File Organization Patterns

### What it is
The standard directory layout for SignalFx Terraform configs at Atlassian.

### How it works

```
<repo-root>/
├── .sauron.yml                          # Sauron config (service_id, TF version, provider versions)
├── bitbucket-pipelines.yml              # Pipeline with sauron-pipe step
└── operations/
    └── terraform/
        ├── main.tf                      # Provider config, module declarations
        ├── sauron.tf                    # Backend HTTP config for state
        ├── variables.tf                 # Variables (team_id, auth tokens, etc.)
        ├── variables_test.tfvars        # Test environment overrides
        ├── locals.tf                    # Computed locals (notification strings)
        └── modules/
            └── detectors/
                ├── detector.p99_escape.tf
                ├── detector.5xx_rate.tf
                └── ...
```

### `.sauron.yml` template
```yaml
---
service_id: "responsible-ai-api"
terraform: operations/terraform
terraform_version: "0.13.4"
sfx_terraform_provider_version: "9.0.0"
tome_terraform_provider_version: "1.6.5"
```

### `sauron.tf` (backend config)
```hcl
terraform {
  backend "http" {
    address = "https://sauron.prod.atl-paas.net/api/state/bitbucket/<workspace>/<repo>"}
  required_providers {
    signalfx = {
      source  = "splunk-terraform/signalfx"
      version = ">= 6.15.0"
    }
    tome = {
      source  = "atlassian/tome"
      version = ">= 1.6.5"
    }
  }
}

provider "signalfx" {
  auth_token     = var.signalfx_auth_token
  api_url        = "https://api.us1.signalfx.com"
  custom_app_url = "https://app.us1.signalfx.com"
}

provider "tome" {
  auth_token = var.tome_auth_token
  host       = var.tome_host
}
```

### `locals.tf` (notification configuration)
```hcl
locals {
  opsgenie_notification = "Opsgenie,${var.opsgenie_credential_id},${var.opsgenie_team_name},${var.opsgenie_team_id},Team"
  slack_notification= "Slack,DxJ_pZzA0N0,${var.slack_alerts_channel}"
}
```

**Source**: [Sauron 101: SignalFX Setup using Terraform](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~510798821/pages/1772291789), [Sauron Onboarding Documentation](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120206523efea921c49908fa9a544a538cf78/pages/5546172795)

