## 7. Development & Testing Workflow

### What it is
The end-to-end workflow from authoring to deployment.

### How it works — Command Surface

| Command | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `sfm --help` | Show SignalFM commands |
| `sfm new` | Bootstrap new project from boilerplate |
| `sfm init` | Initialize terraform with Sauron backend |
| `sfm plan` | Dry-run against production state |
| `sfm apply --create-detectors` | Deploy to test (branch-prefixed) |
| `sfm destroy` | Clean up test resources |
| `terraform fmt<file>` | Format HCL |
| `terraform validate` | Syntax validation |
| `terraform import signalfx_detector.<name> <id>` | Import existing UI detector |
| `terraform state show signalfx_detector.<name>` | Dump detector config |

### Testing Pattern
1. Author `.tf` file
2. `terraform fmt` + `terraform validate` (syntax check)
3. `sfm plan` (dry-run against state, checks for diffs)
4. `sfm apply --create-detectors` (creates test detectors prefixed with alias)
5. Verify in SignalFx UI that detector appears and fires correctly
6. `sfm destroy` (clean up test resources)
7. Create PR → Sauron runs plan on branch → Merge → Sauron applies to production

### Common Errors
| Error | Cause | Fix |
|-------|-------|-----|
| `detect label found in rule wasn't found within program text` | `detect_label` doesn't match `detect().publish()` | Ensure exact string match |
| `Reference to undeclared input variable` | Missing variable | Define in `variables.tf` |
| `detector program text has invalid syntax` | Bad SignalFlow | Test in SignalFx UI first |

**Source**: [How To: Add New SignalFx Detectors in Terraform](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120204aa07fe7450f489899b60900ad6a0967/pages/5977304542), [HOWTO: Terraform SignalFx Set Up](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/uts/pages/5090553860)

