## 5. Key SDK Entry Points & Environment Variables

### `atlassian_ml_studio_sdk.ml_flow.start_mlflow_run`

This is the **recommended** entry point at Atlassian. It:
1. Auto-creates the experiment using standard naming: `/mlflow/{workflow_type}/{region}/{usecase}/{workflow_name}`
2. Shares the same run across all tasks in a workflow run (colocating artifacts, parameters, metrics)
3. Sets `MLFLOW_ENABLE_SYSTEM_METRICS_LOGGING=1` for auto GPU/CPU metrics
4. Handles data residency and workspace configuration boilerplate

```python
from atlassian_ml_studio_sdk.ml_flow import start_mlflow_run
from atlassian_ml_studio_sdk import MLStudioArgumentParser, MLStudioArguments

parser = MLStudioArgumentParser((MLStudioArguments, CustomParams))
mls_args, custom_args, _ = parser.parse_args_into_dataclasses(return_remaining_strings=True)

with start_mlflow_run(mls_args):
    # Experiment and run are auto-configured
    mlflow.log_param("learning_rate", 0.001)
    mlflow.log_metric("accuracy", 0.95)
```

### Environment Variables (auto-set by platform)

| Variable | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `MLFLOW_TRACKING_URI` | Set to `"databricks"` |
| `MLFLOW_RUN_ID` | Parent run ID for the workflow |
| `DATABRICKS_HOST` | Workspace URL |
| `DATABRICKS_TOKEN` | Auth token |
| `MLFLOW_ENABLE_SYSTEM_METRICS_LOGGING` | `1` — auto-logs GPU/CPU |
| `mls_ml_studio_run_id` | ML Studio's internal run ID |
| `mls_workflow_name` | Used for experiment naming |
| `mls_workflow_type` | EXPERIMENTAL, ADHOC, or RELEASED |

### Source
- [ML Studio MLFlow Tracking](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/agd/pages/5795600617)
- [MLflow Integration in Airlock Flows](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/xugc/pages/6659921772)

