## 6. Statistical Significance & Convergence-to-Significance Methodology

### Multi-Seed Aggregation (from autoresearch patterns)
The recommended approach for determining statistical significance of HPO results:
1. **Bootstrap sampling** — Each training run randomly selects 80% of data (training/validation/test) to prevent overfitting hyperparameters to a specific split
2. **Replicate runs** — Multiple runs with identical hyperparameters measure pure error/variance
3. **Response surface regularization** — Replicates help the GP model estimate noise properly

### Convergence Decision Framework (synthesized from Optimus Prime + autoresearch)
```
CONVERGED if ALL of:✓ Convergence plot slope< ε for last N runs (improvements stalled)
  ✓ Predicted optimal config stable (doesn't shift with ±2 data points)
  ✓ Variance at predicted optimum is low
  ✓ Predicted metric ≈ observed metric at predicted config (±5%)
  ✓ No significant surface instability

NOT CONVERGED if ANY of:
  ✗ Surface changes significantly with new data
  ✗ Predicted optimum shifts > 10% on each iteration
  ✗ Fewer than 3-4× dimensions total runs completed
  ✗ All runs cluster in one region (poor exploration)
```

### Bayesian Experimentation Framework (from internal documentation)
For model evaluation significance:
- **Model:** Beta-Binomial per metric
- **Priors:** Derived from historical baselines; N_prior≈ 2-4 weeks of traffic
- **Ship criteria:** P(variant > control) > 95% AND P(relative lift > MDE) > 70-80%
- **Early stop:** If P(variant ≤ control) > 80% for 3+ iterations

