## (h) AI Gateway Routing Config Tool

### What It Is
Configuration tool for AI Gateway model routing across multiple providers (OpenAI, Anthropic, Bedrock, Gemini, TeamServe/internal).

### How It Works

**From [AI Gateway Deep Research Report](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120203d68974c84a8453ab01c35740e7b4416/pages/7068910538) and [Policy-Driven Model Routing](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/7001278725):**

**Supported providers/vendors:**
| Provider | Vendor(s) | Models |
|----------|-----------|--------|
| OpenAI | OpenAI Direct | GPT-5.x, GPT-4.1-mini, o4-mini |
| Anthropic | Bedrock, Vertex AI | Claude Opus4.6, Sonnet 4.5 |
| Google | GCP Vertex | Gemini 3Pro/Flash |
| Amazon | Bedrock | Nova, Llama (Bedrock-hosted) |
| Internal | TeamServe | LLaMA 3.1 8B, GPT-OSS 120B |

**Routing concepts:**
- **Use Case ID:** Every request must include whitelisted `X-Atlassian-UseCaseId`
- **Vendor Policy:** Platform-controlled config determining eligible vendors (`only`, `order`)
- **Model Override:** Transparent substitution (e.g., `gpt-5.3→ gpt-5.4`)
- **Compatibility Groups:** Models across providers sharing same capability tier
- **Fallback Strategy:** `GPT-5.3 → 500 → claude-opus-4-6→ 200✓`
- **Tenant-aware routing:** AHL (Atlassian Hosted) customers → TeamServe only

**Rate limiting in AI Gateway:**
- Per-use-case, per-model TPM limits via Heimdall policies
- Default: 100k TPM per use case
- Priority routing: CRITICAL / HIGH / LOW tiers

**Key response headers:**
- `x-atlassian-serving-model` — actual serving model
- `x-atlassian-requested-model` — original request
- `x-atlassian-model-routing-strategy` — strategy used
- `x-ratelimit-limit` / `retry-after` — rate limit info

**Model tier abstraction (coming M4):**
```yaml
slo-registry:
  entries:
    - tier: PRO
      capability: GENERAL
      models: [gpt-5.3, anthropic.claude-opus-4-6, gemini-3-pro]- tier: STANDARD
      capability: GENERAL
      models: [gpt-5.3, anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-5, gemini-3-flash]
    - tier: LITE
      capability: GENERAL
      models: [gpt-4.1-mini, gemini-3-flash-lite]
```

### How It Applies to Tool

**AI Gateway Routing Config Tool:**
1. `get_use_case_config(use_case_id)` — model, fallback, rate limits, priority
2. `get_model_routing(use_case_id, cloud_id)` — resolved routing chain with tenant restrictions
3. `set_fallback_strategy(use_case_id, fallback_models[], strategy)` — configure cross-vendor fallback
4. `set_model_override(from_model, to_model, scope)` — transparent model substitution
5. `check_routing_health(use_case_id)` — latency, error rates by provider/vendor
6. `kill_switch(use_case_id, action)` — cut traffic by use-case-id during incidents

**Human confirmation required:** Model overrides, kill-switch activation.
**Autonomous:** Reading routing config, checking health, surfacing anomalies.

