# Research Report: rovo-eval/AIX-eval APIs and Evaluation Methodology

## Executive Summary

This report covers the evaluation frameworks (rovo-eval and AIX-eval) available at Atlassian, their APIs, architecture, and the statistical/ML methodology needed for multi-seed aggregation, k-fold/stratified evaluation, slice analysis, calibration metrics (ECE/Brier), fairness metrics (EO/DPD), and bootstrap confidence intervals. The research combines internal Atlassian documentation with industry-standard frameworks and methodologies.

---

## 1. Internal Evaluation Frameworks

### 1.1 AIX-eval (Primary Offline Evaluation Framework)

**What it is:** Atlassian's most mature internal Python-based evaluation framework for LLM/ML quality assessment.

**Package:** `atlassian-ai-experience-evaluation` (aka `aixeval`)  
**Repository:** `bitbucket.org/atlassian/ai-experience-evaluation`  
**Environments:** Local terminal, Databricks notebooks, ML Studio
**Integration:** AI Gateway (model access), MLflow (experiment tracking), Socrates (data versioning)

#### Architecture & API Surface

```python
# Minimal EVaC usage (Evaluations as Code)
from aixeval.workflows.orchestrators import Evaluations
results = await Evaluations.run_async("path/to/your/config.yaml")
```

**CLI Interface:**
```bash
$ aixeval --mode evaluate --config_file config.yaml \--input_output_metrics judge_relevance bleu_metric \
    --log --name experiment_name
```

#### Metric Registry Pattern
- Metrics registered via `@register_metric(metric_type, processing_type)` decorator
- Inherit from abstract `Metric` base class
- Required method: `async compute_on_row(row: pd.Series)` — stateless, per-row
- **8 metric types:** `INPUT_OUTPUT_METRICS`, `OUTPUT_REFERENCE_METRICS`, `INPUT_OUTPUT_REFERENCE_METRICS`, `RETRIEVAL_METRICS`, `INPUT_METRICS`, `OUTPUT_METRICS`, `INPUT_REFERENCE_METRICS`, `DOUBLE_INPUT_OUTPUT_METRICS`
- **Processing modes:** `ASYNC` (LLM judges), `SIMPLE` (pandas apply), `VECTORIZED` (batch)

#### LLM-as-Judge Support
- `LLMJudgeBase` class with multi-iteration scoring
- Score aggregation: mean or majority vote
- `GranularLLMJudge` for per-criterion scoring via Claude tool-use
- `judge_iterations =3` used for reducing LLM variance (per calibration docs)
- Providers: OpenAI, Google (Gemini), Bedrock (Anthropic Claude)

#### Current Metric Library (110+ metrics)
| Category | Examples |
|----------|----------|
| Input+Output | `compression_ratio`, `bleu_metric`, `rouge_metric`, `semantic_similarity`, `bert_score_metric`, `judge_relevance`, `judge_completeness`, `judge_quality` |
| Output-only | `is_only_bullet_points`, `judge_conciseness` |
| Input-only | `word_count`, `token_count` |
| Output+Reference | `judge_coverage` |

#### Key Gaps Identified (Relevant to Skill/Tool)
- **No built-in multi-seed aggregation** — Single-run, no `--repeat N` mode
- **No k-fold/stratified evaluation** — Flat tabular data model, no built-in splitting
- **No calibration metrics** (ECE/Brier) in the metric library
- **No fairness metrics** (EO/DPD) in the metric library
- **No bootstrap CI** computation natively
- **No slice analysis** (SliceLine-style) built in

**Source:** [AIX-Eval Documentation](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120203bd0205883eb4c12af95fe0e997be99f/pages/6522081308/AIX-Eval), [AIX Evals Status Quo & Gap Analysis](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/fde/pages/6983520444/AIX+Evals+Status+Quo+Gap+Analysis), [A guide to efficient LLM evaluations with AIX-eval](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/AM3/pages/3636433645)

