## 2. Alert Configuration — The Trigger Condition Definition

### What it is
ML Lens provides an opt-in alerting system where feature owners register alert configurations via the MLFS SDK. This is the mechanism by which drift thresholds become actionable triggers.

### How it works — AlertConfig SDK Pattern

```python
AlertConfig(alert_namespace="my-team.features", alert_key="drift").alert_message("Drift detected in feature distributions.")
    .runbook("https://go.atlassian.com/my-runbook")
    .alert_config(
        AlertMetricConfig(metric_namespace="feature_observability.drift.ks_pvalue")
        .condition(AlertCondition.single(Condition(measure="expected_value", operator="<=", value=0.05)
        ))
        .tag_filter("feature_name", "=", "daily_transaction_count")
        .tag_filter("feature_service", "=", "fraud_detection_v2")
    )
    .alert_config(
        AlertMetricConfig(metric_namespace="feature_observability.drift.ks_d")
        .condition(AlertCondition.single(
            Condition(measure="expected_value", operator=">=", value=0.1)
        ))
        .tag_filter("feature_name", "=", "daily_transaction_count")
        .tag_filter("feature_service", "=", "fraud_detection_v2")
    ).recipient(Recipient.slack(RecipientValue(id="#ml-alerts", type="channel")))
```

Alert routing targets:
- **Slack** channels
- **JSM Ops** (incident management)

**Source**: [Design: ML Lens Platform Data Drift Detection](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6738511349/Design+ML+Lens+Platform+Data+Drift+Detection), [ML Lens Alerting Requirements](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/5989280688/ML+Lens+Alerting+Requirements)

