## 3. Retraining Trigger Hand-Off Contract — ML Lens → StreamHub → ML Studio Orchestrator

### What it is
The RFC "Model Re-training using Data Quality and ML Lens" defines the event-driven hand-off contract where ML Lens emits drift metrics to StreamHub, which the ML Studio Orchestrator consumes to trigger retraining workflows.

### How it works — The Event Schema (StreamHub Payload)

```json
{
  "$schema": "...",
  "title": "ML Lens Metric",
  "description": "Metrics emitted by ML Lens.",
  "type": "object",
  "required": [
    "ml_studio_run_id",
    "metrics_namespace",
    "metrics",
    "expectations"
  ],
  "properties": {
    "ml_studio_run_id": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "ML Studio run which produced the metrics."
    },
    "tenant_id": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Tenant identifier."
    },
    "region": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Region the workflow ran in."
    },
    "model_id": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Model identifier."
    },
    "product": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Product which produced the metrics."
    },
    "metrics_namespace": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Namespace for the metric."
    },
    "metrics": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Dictionary of metrics (e.g., drift scores)."
    },
    "expectations": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Dictionary of expectations (thresholds)."
    },
