## 5. Drift Metrics Storage Schema

### What it is
The standardized schema for persisting drift metrics, enabling historical analysis and threshold tuning.

### How it works
```sql
core_ml_data.coreml_drift_metrics
├── ds (STRING)                           -- date stamp
├── pipeline_name (STRING)                -- e.g., "rai_moderation_pipeline"
├── model_name (STRING)                   -- e.g., "rai-ft-content-filter-v2-3-3"
├── feature_name (STRING)                 -- NULL for output-level drift
├── drift_test (STRING)                   -- "psi", "ks", "jsd", "chi2", "wasserstein", "cosine"
├── drift_value (DOUBLE)                  -- computed drift statistic
├── drift_threshold_warning (DOUBLE)      -- yellow threshold
├── drift_threshold_error (DOUBLE)        -- red threshold (trigger level)
├── reference_window (STRING)             -- "training", "30d_rolling", "yoy"
├── feature_importance_tier (STRING)      -- SHAP-weighted importance
├── status (STRING)                       -- "OK", "WARNING", "DRIFT"
```

**Source**: [H2 Action Plan: Model Observability & Performance](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DTIE/pages/6495897543/H2+Action+Plan+Model+Observability+Performance)

