## 3. Retraining Trigger Hand-Off Contract — ML Lens → StreamHub → ML Studio Orchestrator

### What it is
The RFC "Model Re-training using Data Quality and ML Lens" defines the event-driven hand-off contract where ML Lens emits drift metrics to StreamHub, which the ML Studio Orchestrator consumes to trigger retraining workflows.

### How it works — The Event Schema (StreamHub Payload)

```json
{
  "$schema": "...",
  "title": "ML Lens Metric",
  "description": "Metrics emitted by ML Lens.",
  "type": "object",
  "required": [
    "ml_studio_run_id",
    "metrics_namespace",
    "metrics",
    "expectations"
  ],
  "properties": {
    "ml_studio_run_id": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "ML Studio run which produced the metrics."
    },
    "tenant_id": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Tenant identifier."
    },
    "region": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Region the workflow ran in."
    },
    "model_id": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Model identifier."
    },
    "product": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Product which produced the metrics."
    },
    "metrics_namespace": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Namespace for the metric."
    },
    "metrics": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Dictionary of metrics (e.g., drift scores)."
    },
    "expectations": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Dictionary of expectations (thresholds)."
    },
    "timestamp": {
      "type": "string",
      "format": "date-time",
      "description": "Timestamp of event."
    }
  }
}
```

Optional fields: `ab_test_id`, `offline_experiment_id`, `tags`, `ml_studio_blueprint_id`, `ml_studio_workflow_id`.

### Trigger Flow (SOP-1 Trigger Phase)

```
1. ML Lens drift computation job runs (every 5 min)
2. Drift metrics computed (KS, PSI, cosine) against reference window
3. Alert evaluation: metrics checked against configured thresholds
4. If threshold breached → ML Lens emits event to StreamHub
5. ML Studio Orchestrator consumes StreamHub event
6. Orchestrator validates re-training conditions (configurable per model)
7. If conditions met → Orchestrator triggers ML Studio workflow
8. ML Studio workflow executes retraining pipeline
```

### Work Plan Milestones (RFC Status)

| Milestone | Description | Status |
|-----------|-------------|--------|
| M1 | Orchestrator listens to events in StreamHub | TO-DO |
| M2 | Re-training using data quality expectations MVP | TO-DO |
| M3 | Announce availability of re-training using data quality | TO-DO |

**Source**: [RFC: Model Re-training using Data Quality and ML Lens](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6013257858/RFC+Model+Re-training+using+Data+Quality+and+ML+Lens)

