## 9. CI/CD Integration — Drift → Retrain → Stage 2 Pipeline

### What it is
The ML Pipeline CI/CD Validation Framework shows how drift detection feeds into the automated retraining loop.

### How it works
```
Drift Monitoring (ML Lens, daily/5-min)
  ├── If drift detected → Trigger Stage 2 pipeline
  │├── Train model (full training pipeline, log to MLflow)
  │     ├── Evaluate model (compare metrics vs thresholds and previous prod model)
  │     ├── Quality gate (block promotion if metrics below threshold)
  │     ├── Register model (version in MLflow registry)
  │     ├── Deploy to staging (serve via FastAPI/BentoML)
  │     ├── Integration tests (validate end-to-end API behaviour)
  │     └── Deploy to production (promote with automatic rollback on failure)
  └── If no drift → Continue scheduled monitoring
```

**Key principle**: Deployment remains **manual** for now (per the RFC), while training and evaluation can be autonomous.

**Source**: [ML Pipeline CI/CD Validation Framework](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~6359788e1cc605b1fd1664ec/pages/6723101866/ML+Pipeline+CI+CD+Validation+Framework+core-ml-batch-pipelines)

