## 7. Integrated Error-Analysis Workflow for SKILL.md

### 7.1 Complete Decision Tree

```
ERROR_ANALYSIS_WORKFLOW:

STEP 1: Data Quality Assessment
  - Run DQ SDK checks (schema, nulls, duplicates, out-of-range)
  - If CRITICAL DQ issues → STOP. Report: "Data Quality Failure"
  - If WARNING-level → log, continue with caution

STEP 2: Distribution Shift Detection
  - Compute PSI/KS for all features vs. reference
  - If significant shift detected:
    - Classify: covariate shift vs concept drift
    - If covariate: check if model output also shifted
    - Report: "Distribution Shift Detected — {type}"

STEP 3: Label Noise Assessment
  - Run CleanLab confident learning on training data
  - If noise_rate > 5%:
    - Report: "Label Noise — {rate}% estimated"
    - Flag top-N suspected mislabeled examples
    - REQUIRE HUMAN REVIEW before correction

STEP 4: Feature Gap Analysis
  - Compute SHAP values
  - Analyze residuals for unexplained patterns
  - If systematic residual patterns found:
    - Report: "Feature Gap — {description}"
    - Suggest candidate features

STEP 5: Model Limitation Diagnosis
  - Compute bias-variance decomposition
  - If high bias (train≈ val, both bad):
    - Report: "Model Limitation — Underfitting"
    - Recommend: more capacity, better architecture- If high variance (train >> val):
    - Report: "Model Limitation — Overfitting"
    - Recommend: regularization, more data, ensembles

STEP 6: Generate Summary Report
  - Root cause classification with confidence
  - Recommended actions ordered by cost/impact
  - Link to monitoring dashboards
```

### 7.2 Human Confirmation Points

The following steps **MUST** require human confirmation:
- Label corrections (never auto-correct labels)
- Model retraining decisions (drift detected → retrain)
- Feature engineering changes (new features may have compliance implications)
- Alert threshold changes

The following can be **autonomous**:
- Running detection algorithms
- Computing metrics and generating reports
- Logging results to metric stores
- Sending notifications/alerts

### 7.3 Key Domain Terminology for AI Understanding

| Term | Definition |
|------|-----------|
| PSI | Population Stability Index — measures distribution divergence |
| KS Test | Kolmogorov-Smirnov test — max difference between CDFs |
| Covariate Shift | P(X) changes but P(Y|X) remains stable |
| Concept Drift | P(Y|X) changes — the fundamental relationship shifts |
| Confident Learning | Algorithm to estimate label noise using model predictions |
| Label Quality Score | Per-example score indicating likelihood of correct labeling |
| SHAP | SHapley Additive exPlanations — feature attribution method |
| ECE | Expected Calibration Error — measures prediction confidence reliability |
| Domain Classifier | Binary classifier trained to distinguish reference vs. current data |
| Feature Drift | Change in distribution of a single input feature |
| Dataset Drift | Aggregate measure across all features |

