### (f) Responsible-AI-API Ops Runbook Skill + Two-Stage Moderation Pipeline Operations Tool

| Aspect | Detail |
|--------|--------|
| **Gap** | The primary runbook is ~470 days stale. The two-stage moderation pipeline (LLaMA 3.1 8B / Gemma 4→ GPT-OSS Safeguard 20B) is being designed but has no operational tool for the AI employee to manage it. |
| **What exists** | Architecture design for two-stage pipeline: Stage 1 (fast, ~200ms, ~100% recall, ~2% blocking) → Stage 2 (precise, >95% precision, re-evaluates only Stage 1 DISALLOW). Feature gates control model selection (`rai_api_enable_gptoss_safeguard`). Four endpoints: prompt, agent, image, output moderation. |
| **Justification** | Two components: (1) A **skill** encoding the ops runbook for responsible-ai-api (endpoint health checks, escalation paths, common failure modes, remediation steps, freshness footer). (2) A **tool** for pipeline operations: query current moderation pipeline state (which model active per stage), check blocking rates, check fail-open status across all4 endpoints, trigger shadow-testing for new model versions. |
| **Human confirmation** | Model swap (stage promotion): REQUIRED. Read pipeline state: autonomous. Shadow test initiation: autonomous. |
| **Source** | [Two-Stage Prompt Moderator Architecture](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120202437cfa6229b4f95a58ffcf2c483eb04/pages/7064183361), [Responsible-AI-API: Model Overview](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120209f2f166a31fb4c7e9508d87165eba912/pages/6869413493), [responsible-ai-api Optimization](https://hello.jira.atlassian.cloud/browse/AI-262) |

