### (g) Per-Tenant Token-Bucket Rate-Limit Configurator Tool

| Aspect | Detail |
|--------|--------|
| **Gap** | No rate limiting currently exists on `/v1/moderation/image` (confirmed: `grep -nr "rate_limit\|token_bucket" src/api/v1/moderation/image_moderation_controller.py` returns nothing). A single tenant triggered8,251 errors/min, exhausting SageMaker workers. |
| **What exists** | The pattern is well-established at Atlassian (Heimdall/Hofund for distributed rate limiting, token-bucket algorithm). The responsible-ai-api needs an in-process token-bucket keyed on `tenant_id`. Feature gate planned (`default-off`). |
| **Justification** | A new **tool** is needed that: (1) reads current rate-limit configuration per tenant, (2) adjusts token-bucket capacity and refill rate for specific tenants, (3) surfaces rate-limit metrics (`image_moderation_rate_limited` with tenant_id tag), (4) can emergency-adjust limits without redeploy (via dynamic config). |
| **Human confirmation** | Adjusting limits: REQUIRED (prevents accidental tenant lockout). Reading current config: autonomous. |
| **Source** | [OPP-202605-03](https://hello.jira.atlassian.cloud/browse/AI-263), [Burst API rate limiting](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/BRL/pages/5335241828) |

