| **Gap** | AI Gateway manages300-400+ use cases with routing to OpenAI, Anthropic (Bedrock+Vertex), Google Gemini, and internal models (TeamServe). Configuration is via Heimdall policies (~400KB file), `models.yml`, and feature flags. No agent-facing tool exists to query or modify routing. |
| **What exists** | V1 provider-specific endpoints + V2 unified `/v2/chat`. Fallback strategies (DEFAULT, LLAMA_70B, GPT_OSS_20B_TS, GPT_OSS_120B_TS, NONE, ENFORCED). Circuit breaker per use-case/model. Shipyard replacing mlp-config. Policy-Driven Model Routing engineering plan (May 2026). |
| **Justification** | A new **tool** is needed that: (1) queries current routing configuration for a use-case (which models, which fallback chain, which vendor policy), (2) reads circuit breaker state per use-case/model, (3) can trigger fallback strategy changes for incident response (e.g., force all traffic to TeamServe), (4) reads Gemini smart routing state (PT utilization, overflow to Priority). |
| **Human confirmation** | Route changes: REQUIRED (affects all AI traffic). Reading config: autonomous. Emergency fallback activation: REQUIRED but with fast-path (single confirmation). |
| **Source** | [AI Gateway Internal LLMs Routing](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/5871499558), [AI Gateway Deep Research Report](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120203d68974c84a8453ab01c35740e7b4416/pages/7068910538), [Policy-Driven Model Routing](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/7001278725), [Heimdall scaling](https://hello.jira.atlassian.cloud/browse/COMMIT-24446) |

