## 2. Capability Gap Analysis — Justification for New Tools/Skills

### (a) ML Lens Query Tool — Drift Metrics

| Aspect | Detail |
|--------|--------|
| **Gap** | No existing MCP tool wraps the ML Lens Query API or Metrics API for on-demand queries. The AI employee cannot currently ask "What is the KS drift score for feature X in the last 24h?" |
| **What exists** | ML Lens has an HTTP Query API (StarRocks-backed), a Metrics API, and alert evaluation. But these are internal service APIs with no agent-facing tool. |
| **Missing metric types** | KL divergence and cosine similarity for NLP embeddings are not yet computed by ML Lens (only KS and PSI). The ≥0.60 NLP floor needs custom thresholds. |
| **Justification** | A new **tool** is needed that wraps the ML Lens Query API to: (1) query drift metrics by namespace/feature/window, (2) apply NLP-specific thresholds (cosine ≥0.60), (3) return structured dashboard-like summaries (data-quality, model-perf, system-health). |
| **Human confirmation** | Read-only queries — no confirmation needed. |
| **Source** | [ML Lens Query API](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/5937111395), [Option 1: StarRocks Deep Drift Analysis](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6949715806) |

---

### (b) SignalFx Detectors-as-Code Authoring Tool + Per-Endpoint SLOs

| Aspect | Detail |
|--------|--------|
| **Gap** | No tool generates valid Terraform HCL for `signalfx_detector` resources or Tome SLO definitions. Currently0 detectors exist in the responsible-ai-api IaC (`grep -c "signalfx_detector" operations/terraform/*.tf == 0`). |
| **What exists** | Sauron pipeline deploys Terraform on merge to master. SignalFM exports existing detectors. But no tool *authors new detectors* from specifications. |
| **Justification** | A new **tool** is needed that: (1) generates `signalfx_detector` Terraform HCL from a detector specification (metric, threshold, duration, severity, notifications), (2) generates Tome SLO capability definitions, (3) validates against SignalFlow syntax, (4) creates PRs to the operations/terraform/ directory. |
| **Human confirmation** | REQUIRED — PR review before merge (Sauron only applies on master). |
| **Source** | [OPP-202605-04](https://hello.jira.atlassian.cloud/browse/AI-264), [STRA-202605-06](https://hello.jira.atlassian.cloud/browse/AI-264), [Sauron SignalFX Howto](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ATF/pages/1059524356) |

---

### (c) Drift-Triggered Retraining Trigger Skill (SOP-1)

| Aspect | Detail |
|--------|--------|
| **Gap** | ML Lens has alerting but no automated retraining trigger. The RFC for "Model Re-training using Data Quality and ML Lens" exists but is not implemented. |
| **What exists** | ML Lens can evaluate drift thresholds and emit alerts. ML Studio can run training workflows. But the linkage (drift alert → retraining job trigger) is manual today. |
| **Justification** | A new **skill** (SKILL.md workflow) is needed that encodes the SOP-1 trigger phase: (1) receive drift alert (KS/PSI/cosine above threshold), (2) validate alert is sustained (not transient), (3) check if retraining is already in-flight, (4) trigger ML Studio retraining blueprint via API, (5) post status to Slack, (6) create tracking Jira issue. |
| **Human confirmation** | REQUIRED at step4 — retraining has cost and risk implications. |
| **Source** | [RFC: Model Re-training using Data Quality and ML Lens](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6013257858) |

