### (d) Circuit-Breaker Controller Skill + Tool (20%/60s window, fail-open kill-switch)

| Aspect | Detail |
|--------|--------|
| **Gap** | The responsible-ai-api has circuit breakers on prompt/output moderation but NOT on agent moderation. No existing tool can read CB state, toggle kill-switches, or configure thresholds. |
| **What exists** | Feature gates in `feature_service.py` (e.g., `should_fail_open_on_model_timeout()`, `should_fail_open_if_circuit_breaker_open()`). Resilience4j-style patterns. Kill-switch gates (default-off). The codebase uses `inference_error_handler()` context manager. |
| **Justification** | Two components needed: (1) A **tool** that can read/write circuit breaker configuration (threshold=20%, window=60s, current state), toggle the fail-open kill-switch gate, and emit the `agent_moderation_fail_open` metric status. (2) A **skill** encoding the SOP for when to engage/disengage the CB and kill-switch (automated vs. human-confirmed scenarios). |
| **Human confirmation** | Kill-switch toggle: REQUIRED. CB threshold adjustment: REQUIRED. Reading CB state: autonomous. |
| **Source** | [AI-206: Add fail-open/circuit breaker to agent moderation](https://hello.jira.atlassian.cloud/browse/AI-206), [OPP-202605-02](https://hello.jira.atlassian.cloud/browse/AI-266) |

