1. Role-doc requirements (extracted from §2.4, §3.1, §4.3, §5.1, §6.2 step 4,
§7.1, §9, §11.1, §11.3): Tecton/MLFS lifecycle covers 5 stages — generated → 
written → hydrated → logged (with request_id) → joined with labels. DQ
obligations are coverage / sparsity / freshness audits partitioned by
connector × region × tenant, required before SOP-2 training. Autonomy tiers:
🟢 consume features; 🟡 new pipeline; 🔴 schema changes affecting consumers.

2. Existing local tool/skill inventory — no first-class coverage exists.

 • Closest substrate: socrates_* MCP (SQL async + status) — covers ~30% of DQ
   via raw SQL only.
 • Adjacent reusable surfaces: bitbucket* (feature definitions as
   code-as-config + PR mutation), compass (service dependencies for lineage
   padding), twg/teamwork_graph (cross-product context/lineage), atlassian
   (Jira/Confluence paperwork for 🟡/🔴 escalations), slack (sustained-error
   alerting), SRE prometheus_query/alertmanager_query/log_query (freshness lag
   plumbing).
 • NO tooling exists for: Tecton DSL, FeatureView define/plan/apply, online
   hydration, point-in-time-correct historical joins, schema-diff,
   online↔offline consistency check, freshness lag with SLA registry, sparsity
   CIs, or --gate mode for pre-training blocking.

3. Gap-justified net-new tools (both qualify per parent-task mandate):

 • mlfs — Tecton/MLFS client (define, plan/apply, write, get_online_features,
   get_historical_features-PIT, lineage, schema_diff) with embedded
   autonomy-tier gates.
 • feature_dq_audit — coverage/sparsity/freshness auditor with partition
   fan-out, statistical CIs, freshness-SLA registry, --gate exit-code contract
   for SOP-2.

4. Cross-cluster shared-infra wrapper check: Tecton ❌, MLFS ❌, Unity Catalog
❌ (proxied via Socrates), Socrates ✅ (reuse), MLflow ❌ (out of scope here),
Argo ❌.

5. Integration patterns documented: (A) SOP-2 step 4 pre-training DQ gate
composing feature_dq_audit → atlassian + slack; (B) SOP-1 step 1 drift
correlation composing ml_lens + mlfs lineage + bitbucket commit history + twg;
(C) Schema-change 🔴 escalation composing mlfs schema_diff + compass deps +
atlassian + bitbucket PR/pipeline.

6. AI-autonomy considerations captured: tier-aware write gates, plan/apply
separation (Terraform-style), calibrated-uncertainty CIs and explicit
"insufficient data" signal, fail-open --fallback for hydrate path,
retry/backoff for Tecton + obedience to socrates_get_query_status polling,
cross-tenant publish guard, ORBIT-ingestible reasoning traces on every gate
decision.


Bottom-line: Both mlfs and feature_dq_audit are net-new with strong
justification; major savings come from reusing socrates_*, atlassian, slack,
bitbucket, twg, compass, and future Cluster A signalfx_detectors_as_code
rather than reimplementing them.
