## (h) AI Gateway Routing Config Tool

### What It Is
A tool that manages AI Gateway model routing configuration: provider selection, fallback chains, vendor policies, model overrides, and feature-gate-controlled routing decisions across OpenAI/Anthropic/Bedrock/Gemini/internal (TeamServe/MSP).

### How It Works (from internal docs)

**Routing Architecture** (from [AI Gateway Internal LLMs Routing](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/5871499558) and [Policy-Driven Model Routing](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/7001278725)):

**Entry Points**:
1. `/v1/openai/v1/chat/completions` — OpenAI-compatible with fallback logic
2. `/v1/teamserve/{modelId}` — Direct internal model access
3. `/v2/chat` — Unified API (model-agnostic, recommended for new callers)

**Routing Decision Matrix**:
| CloudID Type | Organization Control | Result |
|-------------|---------------------|--------|
| Internal-Only | `atlassianHostedLLMs = true` | ALLOWED internal, BLOCKED external |
| Feature Flag Blocked | Blocking enabled | ALLOWED internal, BLOCKED external |
| Standard | No restrictions | ALLOWED all routes |

**Fallback Strategy Options**:
1. DEFAULT → TeamServe
2. LLAMA_70B → `llama-3-3-70b-instruct-ts`
3. GPT_OSS_20B_TS → GPT-OSS 20B with Harmony format
4. GPT_OSS_120B_TS → GPT-OSS 120B with Harmony format
5. NONE → No fallback
6. ENFORCED → Gemini fallback

**Vendor Configuration** (from [ADR: Shipyard for AI Gateway Config](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6619605534)):
- 204 models in production across 7 vendors: ANTHROPIC, BEDROCK, FIREWORKS, GOOGLE, MSP, OPENAI, TEAMSERVE
- 7 categories: EMBEDDING, LLM, MODERATION, RERANK, STT, TTI, TTS
- Config stored via Shipyard (replacing mlp-config)

**Policy-Driven Routing** (from [Engineering Overview](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/7001278725)):
```
Component requests: tier=STANDARD, capability=GENERAL, preferred_model=gpt-5.3
Tenant config: allowed_providers = ["anthropic", "google"]

Step 1 — SLO Lookup:    [gpt-5.3, claude-sonnet-4-5, gemini-3-flash, gpt-4.1]
Step 2 — Tenant Filter:  ✗ gpt-5.3 (openai)✓ claude-sonnet-4-5  ✓ gemini-3-flash
Step 3 — Preference:     gpt-5.3 not in candidates → ignore
Step 4 — Fallback chain: primary=claude-sonnet-4-5, fallback=gemini-3-flash
```

**Smart Routing** (from [Gemini Smart Routing](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6523243927)):
- Provisioned Throughput (PT) → Priority Tier → Standard PAYG
- External requests prioritized to dedicated tier
- Internal requests may overflow to standard tier during peak

