## (g) Per-Tenant Token-Bucket Rate-Limit Configurator Tool

### What It Is
A tool that configures per-tenant, per-model TPM (tokens per minute) rate limits for the AI Gateway and responsible-ai-api services using the Heimdall policy framework and token-bucket algorithm.

### How It Works (from internal docs)

**Current State** (from [AA-504: Per-Tenant AI Token Rate Limiter](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020764635251a61463aab16223409221de5/pages/6828203194)):
- AI Gateway has service-level TPM limit of 300K
- **No per-tenant rate limiting exists** — noisy tenant can starve all others
- Pattern to follow: Email Rate Limiter (per-tenant, DynamoDB-backed, production-proven)

**Token Bucket Algorithm** (from [Burst API Rate Limiting HLD](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/BRL/pages/5399334316)):
- Each tenant+API combination gets its own token bucket
- Capacity: maximum burst tokens
- Refill rate: tokens per second
- When bucket empty → HTTP 429
- Bucket refills automatically at steady rate

**Heimdall Policy Structure** (from [Partner Rate Limiting](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~63da235efb75f8568f5f6e37/pages/5289122309)):
```yaml
- key: artifact
  value: <use-case-id>
  descriptors:
  - key: client
    rate_limit:- requests_per_unit: 300000# TPM
      unit: minutedescriptors:
    - key: user# per-tenant
      value: <tenant-id>
      rate_limit:
      - requests_per_unit: 50000  # per-tenant TPM
        unit: minute
```

**AI Gateway Scaling Challenge** (from [COMMIT-24446](https://hello.jira.atlassian.cloud/browse/COMMIT-24446)):
- 300-400+ use cases managed today
- Policy file already ~400KB in production
- Configuration explosion as models/versions grow
- Need: per-use-case, per-model, per-tenant limits

**Rate Limit Tiers** (from [OPP-202605-03]):
- Per-tenant rate limiting on `/v1/moderation/image` specifically called out as priority item
- Existing metric: `ai-gateway.unified-chat.total.token` already tracks per-request token usage

### Tool Specification

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| **Name** | `rate-limit-configurator` |
| **Purpose** | Configure per-tenant token-bucket rate limits for AI Gateway endpoints; adjust TPM caps; manage noisy-tenant isolation |
| **Autonomy Tier** | 🟡 Human-confirm (rate limit changes impact production traffic) |
| **Leveraged Tools** | Heimdall policy API, DynamoDB (token bucket state), AI Gateway metrics (Splunk/SignalFx) |
| **New-Tool Justification** | Currently no per-tenant limiting exists; manual Heimdall config is error-prone at400+ use cases; AI can generate correct policy YAML |
| **Inputs** | `tenant_id`, `use_case_id`, `model_id`, `tpm_limit`, `bucket_capacity`, `refill_rate` |
| **Outputs** | Updated policy YAML, validation result, current_usage_vs_limit metrics |
| **SOP Linkage** | §3.2 AI Gateway rate limiting; §5.1 capacity management; §9 noisy-tenant challenge |

