## Cross-Cutting Patterns & Recommendations

### Autonomy Tier Framework

| Tier | Symbol | Meaning | Items |
|------|--------|---------|-------|
| Fully Autonomous | 🟢 | No human approval needed; read-only or low-risk | (a) drift queries, (d) monitoring, (e) Slack ack + cross-correlation |
| Human-Confirm | 🟡 | AI prepares action, human approves | (b) detector PR, (c) retraining trigger, (d) kill-switch, (f) config changes, (g) rate limits, (h) routing changes |
| Human-Required | 🔴 | Must not execute without explicit human instruction | (d) kill-switch activation during active incident |

### Common Tooling Dependencies

1. **Switcheroo/Statsig** — Feature gates and kill-switches (items d, f, h)
2. **SignalFx** — Metrics and detectors (items a, b, d, e)
3. **Slack API** — Notifications and incident channels (items c, e)
4. **Heimdall** — Rate limiting policies (item g)
5. **Shipyard** — AI Gateway configuration (item h)
6. **ML Lens Query API** — Drift metrics (items a, c)
7. **JSM Ops** — Incident management (item e)
8. **Bitbucket** — IaC PRs (item b)

