## 5. Permissions Model

### 5.1 Permission Types
- **Owner**: AD group that owns the component/namespace
- **Writers**: Who can upload artifacts and create versions
  - AD groups
  - ASAP issuers (service-to-service)
  - Bitbucket Pipelines build identities (`pipelinesBuild:{repo-uuid}`)
- **Readers**: Who can download artifacts (default: open to all authenticated)
- **Deployers**: Who can deploy artifacts (relevant for UGC models)

### 5.2 SDK Permission Management
```python
from atlassian_msp_sdk import ml_registry

# Update permissions on component
ml_registry.update_component_permissions(
    "my-namespace.MyComponent",
    permissions={
        "writers": ["ad-group:ml-team", "asap:ml-studio/my_workflow/released"],
        "deployers": ["service:my-production-service"]
    }
)
```

### 5.3 Authentication Principals

| Principal Type | Example | Compliance |
|---------------|---------|------------|
| ASAP issuer | `micros/<service>`, `ml-studio/<usecase>/<workflow_type>` | Depends on workflow type |
| Bitbucket Pipeline | `pipelinesBuild:{repo-uuid}` | Only if SOX-controlled branch |
| AD employee | Staff via `atlas slauth curl` | Always non-compliant |
| AD group | Group membership | Inherited from member type |

