## Finding 9: Data Quality Observability Dashboard Pattern

### What It Is
The AI DE Data Quality Observability Dashboard (AIDE-421) defines the standard metrics taxonomy for DQ monitoring.

### Dashboard Metrics Relevant to Coverage/Sparsity/Freshness:

| Metric Category | Specific Metrics |
|---|---|
| **Completeness** | Row-level completeness per partition, null/blank rate per critical column with thresholds |
| **Freshness** | Max lag between latest record timestamp and current time per table/topic, staleness alerts |
| **Volume/Anomaly** | Daily row counts with historical baselines and anomaly flags |
| **Schema Changes** | Schema evolution events, compatibility status |

**Dashboard Views:**
- **Executive View:** High-level health score per domain, per AI use case
- **Team View:** Per-pipeline DQ metrics, backlog of failures
- **Drill-Down:** Table/column-level metric history with filters by **domain** and **owner**

### How It Applies

The skill/tool should emit metrics compatible with this dashboard pattern:
- Per-partition health scores rolled up to Feature View level
- DoD/WoW trend tracking (already implemented in Feature DQ pipeline)
- Drill-down by connector → region → tenant

