## Finding 10: Error Detection & Drift Patterns (Adjacent to DQ)

### What It Is
Beyond static threshold checks, ML feature DQ requires distribution shift detection — identifying when a connector's data characteristics change over time.

### Patterns From Internal Research:

**TOFU Quality Pipeline Investigation** found:
- Null rates increasing from 6.91% → 12.74% for web visit features over 6 months
- Feature columns degrading per-connector without triggering aggregate alerts
- Solution: track null rates **per dimension** over time, alert on **trend changes** not just absolute thresholds

**ML DQ SDK Drift Metrics:**
- PSI (Population Stability Index) for distribution shift
- KS (Kolmogorov-Smirnov) test for statistical significance
- These should be computed **per partition** to catch connector-specific drift

### How It Applies

The skill/tool should include a "drift-aware" mode:
1. Store historical metric values per partition (baseline)
2. Compare current metrics to rolling baseline
3. Alert when a partition's coverage/sparsity trends worsen significantly even if still within absolute thresholds
4. This catches "slow degradation" patterns (e.g., a connector gradually losing data)

### Source
- [TOFU Quality Pipeline -- Prediction Quality Investigation](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020e1ab777b4d3445cba5b4529eaa858820/pages/6545029859)
- [ML Observability for Growth Recommendations](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/KYC/pages/6650192184)

