└────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────┘
                         │
                         ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Stage 2: Validate (threshold application)           │
│  - Compare metrics to configured thresholds          │
│  - Derive SUCCESS/FAILURE/BOOTSTRAP per partition    │
│  - Write to DQ fact table                            │
└────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────┘
                         │
                         ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Stage 3: Report & Alert│
│  - Aggregate health per Feature View                 │
│  - Slack notification on failures                    │
│  - Dashboard with DoD/WoW trends                     │
│  - MLflow logging of DQ metrics                      │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Key Design Decisions

| Decision | Recommendation | Rationale |
|---|---|---|
| Primary engine | Great Expectations v1.x | Atlassian standard; best metric output quality |
| Freshness implementation | Rule-based custom function (not GX) | GX has no native freshness |
| Partitioning strategy | Pre-filter DataFrame + `row_condition` | Proven pattern inFinOps framework |
| Configuration format | YAML with SQL auto-discovery | Balance of readability and flexibility |
| Result schema | 15-column uniform schema | Compatible with existingFinOps rollup |
| Alerting | Slack Block Kit + ML Lens | Existing infrastructure |
| Human confirmation required | Threshold setting, severity assignment | Domain expertise needed |
| Autonomous execution | Running checks, computing metrics, writing results | Safe, repeatable operations |

### Terminology the AI Must Understand

| Term | Definition |
|---|---|
| **Coverage** | Proportion of non-null values in a column (= 1 - null_rate) |
| **Sparsity** | Proportion of zero-valued rows for numeric features |
| **Freshness** | Time elapsed since the most recent data point (hours/days) |
| **Partition dimension** | A categorical column used to slice DQ metrics (connector_type, region, tenant_tier) |
| **Health grading** | HEALTHY (all pass) / DEGRADED (medium/low fail) / UNAVAILABLE (high-severity fail) |
| **Feature View** | A Tecton/MLFS construct defining a set of ML features materialized from source data |
| **row_condition** | A Spark SQL expression used to filter rows before applying a GX expectation |
| **BOOTSTRAP** | Status for volume checks with insufficient history (< 2 days) — no alert |

