# Symphony Governance + Day-One Bootstrap Stack — Deep Research Findings

## Executive Summary

This research covers the full "Cluster H" stack for AI Employee governance: Symphony Orchestrator lifecycle, ORBIT read/write, policy compliance with autonomy tiers, calibrated uncertainty, audit-log emitters, and Day-One bootstrap. All findings are sourced from internal Atlassian documentation (Confluence pages last updated March–May 2026) describing the architecture being built for the AI Employee Strategy.

---

## (i) Symphony Orchestrator — Lifecycle Interface Skill

### What It Is

Atlassian Symphony is the agent orchestration layer that turns work surfaces (Jira, JSM, Opsgenie, ML pipelines) into a continuous control plane for AI employees. It implements a six-phase lifecycle loop: **Watch → Bootstrap → Execute → Supervise → Close → Learn**.

**Source:** [Atlassian Symphony: AI Employee Orchestration Platform](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202027e1af5d30e94112880666ee62f9277a/pages/6933824809) | [AI Employee Strategy](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202027e1af5d30e94112880666ee62f9277a/pages/6742955831)

### How It Works — The Six Lifecycle Phases

| Phase | What Happens | Inputs | Outputs | Human Role |
|-------|-------------|--------|---------|------------|
| **Watch** | Continuously polls control planes (JSM, Jira boards, ML experiment queues) for new work items | Control plane API (JQL eligibility query, Opsgenie alerts, ML queue) | Detected work items; eligibility evaluation | Sets scope and policy; Symphony handles watching |
| **Bootstrap** | Spawns a dedicated AI employee agent per work item; ORBIT loads a context pack scoped to the task | Work item metadata + ORBIT Context Pack API call | Running agent instance with full domain context | No action needed — automatic |
| **Execute** | Agent runs within policy-scoped workspace; takes autonomous actions for known patterns; escalates at policy boundaries | Agent runtime (OpenClaw/Rovo Dev), policy enforcement layer, reasoning traces | Work artifacts (PRs, incident resolutions, experiment results) | Reviews escalations at policy boundaries |
| **Supervise** | Monitors agent health; restarts stalled/crashed agents; preserves work item ownership across restarts | Agent health signals, heartbeats, timeout thresholds | Restart signals, ownership preservation records | Receives escalations when agents hit policy boundaries |
| **Close** | Agent delivers output; reasoning trace captured for review | Completed work artifact, proof-of-work evidence | Closed work item + reasoning trace + output artifact | Reviews outcomes and reasoning traces |
| **Learn** | Completed work item enriches ORBIT context layer for that scope | Task outcome, agent execution logs, domain knowledge extracted | Updated ORBIT context (appended learnings) | No action needed — automatic |

### Architecture (from OpenAI Symphony + Atlassian adaptation)

**OpenAI Symphony (upstream reference):**
- Written in **Elixir/OTP** for fault-tolerant supervision
- **Supervisor tree**: Application → PubSub → Task.Supervisor → WorkflowStore → Orchestrator (GenServer) → HttpServer → StatusDashboard
- **Orchestration cycle**: Tick → Fetch → Reconcile → Dispatch → Retry
- **State model**: In-memory (restart recovery re-reads issue tracker state)
- **WORKFLOW.md**: Policy-as-code config file (YAML front matter + Markdown prompt template)

**Atlassian Symphony adaptation:**
- Watches Jira + JSM + ML platform instead of Linear
- Bootstraps with ORBIT context packs instead of raw workspace
- Integrates with OpenClaw/Rovo Dev as agent runtime
- Policy enforcement:🟢/🟡/🔴 autonomy model
- Reasoning traces captured per agent run

### WORKFLOW.md — The Configuration Contract

Every Symphony deployment is governed by a `WORKFLOW.md` file with:
- **YAML front matter**: Typed runtime config — tracker settings, workspace root, concurrency limits, sandbox policy, lifecycle hooks
- **Markdown body**: Prompt template sent to the agent at session start

```yaml
tracker:
  kind: jira
  project_key: $JIRA_PROJECT_KEY
  api_token: $JIRA_API_TOKEN
  base_url: $JIRA_BASE_URL
  eligibility_jql: "label = agent-ready AND status = 'To Do' AND storyPoints <= 5"
workspace:
  root: $SYMPHONY_WORKSPACE_ROOT
agent:
  command: "acli rovodev run"
concurrency:
  max_runs: 3
hooks:
  after_create: |
    git clone --depth 1 "$BITBUCKET_REPO_URL" .
    git checkout -b agent/$ISSUE_KEY
```

**Source:** [Symphony for Atlassian: Rovo Dev + Jira + Bitbucket Architecture](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020e062b0af65f448f7a62e88cdc9102c6f/pages/6615014652) | [WORKFLOW.md Schema Specification](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020e062b0af65f448f7a62e88cdc9102c6f/pages/6623694357)

### How to Encode as a Skill (SKILL.md)

The Symphony Orchestrator interface skill should encode:

1. **Phase entry/exit callbacks** — Each phase transition triggers a hook. The skill guides the agent on what to emit and check at each boundary.
2. **Watch configuration** — JQL eligibility rules, polling intervals, control plane selection per role.
3. **Bootstrap contract** — Invoking ORBIT Context Pack API with correct purpose (`AGENT_EXECUTE`), loading context, confirming readiness.
4. **Execute guardrails** — Policy enforcement hooks (🟢 proceed / 🟡 confirm / 🔴 escalate), reasoning trace capture.
5. **Supervise health protocol** — Heartbeat emission, stall detection thresholds, restart-with-state-preservation.
6. **Close ceremony** — Proof-of-work validation, output delivery, reasoning trace finalization.
7. **Learn append** — Writing completed task learnings back to ORBIT.

**Human confirmation required at:** Phase transitions from Execute to Close (when policy hits🟡/🔴); any escalation event; agent restart after failure.

