## (vi) Day-One Bootstrap Skill

### What It Is

The Day-One bootstrap skill orchestrates the complete onboarding of a new AI employee instance: access provisioning (§11.1), document ingestion (§11.2), and first tasks (§11.3, tasks 5–6). It ensures the agent is productive from its first work item.

**Source:** [Agentic Operations in the New SDLC](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202027e1af5d30e94112880666ee62f9277a/pages/6885869718) | [Digital TPM: AI Employee Vision](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202027e1af5d30e94112880666ee62f9277a/pages/6900978790) | [DRAFT AI-Lab — Hire an AI Employee for Your Repo](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/LAB/pages/6857153393)

### §11.1 Access Provisioning

On instantiation, the AI employee needs:
- **Identity**: Agent account with AAID (lazy provisioning on first autonomous invocation)
- **Permissions**: Role-based access (PRODUCT_MEMBER), scoped to assigned service/repo/team
- **Tool access**: MCP tools, API tokens (Jira, Confluence, Bitbucket, Slack)
- **Workspace**: Isolated filesystem for code operations
- **Credentials**: OBO (On-Behalf-Of) token exchange for delegated authorization

### §11.2 Document Ingestion

Bootstrap Training ingests (from "Agentic Operations in the New SDLC"):
1. **ORBIT context pack** — ML-ranked view of what's active, at-risk, and owned
2. **Service Spec (Intent Map)** — Canonical description of what the service does
3. **Incident history** — Past HOTs, postmortems, Causal Graphs, Permanent Remediation PRs
4. **Runbooks and policy expressions** — Human-authored playbooks → machine-executable policies
5. **Observability config** — Alert definitions, SLO thresholds, dashboard layouts

### §11.3 First Tasks (Tasks 5–6)

If documentation is good → agent is productive on Day1.
If documentation is poor → agent's first job is **documentation audit**:
- Read the code
- Query the graph
- Fill in knowledge gaps
- Generate missing runbooks/specs

**The "Hire via URL" pattern:**
1. User tells coding agent to "follow [URL] to hire an AI-employee"
2. Agent follows instructions to set up: `agents.md` (and related `.md`), local tools, telemetry hooks
3. Every new session start → agent offers to update from central prototype
4. Learnings sent back to server after each session (opt-in)

### Bootstrap Sequence (full workflow)

```
1. INSTANTIATION├── Create agent identity (AAID)
   ├── Assign to scope (service/repo/team)
   ├── Provision tool access (MCP, APIs)
   └── Create isolated workspace

2. CONTEXT LOADING (§11.2)
   ├── Call ORBIT Context Pack API (purpose: AGENT_BOOTSTRAP)
   ├── Ingest service spec / intent map
   ├── Load incident history
   ├── Parse runbooks → executable policies
   └── Import observability config (SLOs, alerts, dashboards)

3. VALIDATION
   ├── Verify all access works (tool health checks)
   ├── Confirm context is sufficient (coverage audit)
   ├── If gaps found → generate documentation (first task)
   └── Report readiness to Symphony

4. FIRST TASKS (§11.3)
   ├── Task 5: Documentation audit + gap filling
   ├── Task 6: First operational task (monitoring check, code review, etc.)
   └── Emit "bootstrap complete" audit event

5. ENTER ACTIVE OPS
   └── Transition to Watch phase for continuous operation
```

### How to Encode as a Skill

The Day-One bootstrap skill is a **one-time initialization workflow** that runs before the agent enters its normal Symphony loop:

```
PRE-REQUISITES:
- Agent role defined (SRE/SWE/MLE/TPM)
- Scope assigned (service, repo, or team)
- Orchestrator (Symphony) has spawned the agent

STEPS:
1. [AUTONOMOUS] Verify identity and access- Check AAID is provisioned
   - Verify tool access (API connectivity tests)
   - Confirm workspace exists and is writable
2. [AUTONOMOUS] Load ORBIT context
   - GET /orbit/context?purpose=AGENT_BOOTSTRAP&scope={assigned_scope}
   - Parse and index entities by layer
   - Identify primary work items (Inner orbit)
3. [AUTONOMOUS] Ingest domain documents
   - Load service spec from Confluence (if exists)
   - Load incident history from JSM
   - Load runbooks from linked documentation
   - Import observability config (SLO definitions, alert rules)
   
4. [AUTONOMOUS] Assess readiness
   - Score context completeness (0-100%)
   - Identify critical gaps
   - If gaps > threshold → first task = documentation generation
5. [REQUIRES CONFIRMATION] Report to human
   - Present: "I'm ready to start. Here's what I know about {scope}."
   - List: context loaded, gaps identified, proposed first action
   - Await: Human confirmation to proceed
   
6. [AUTONOMOUS] Execute first tasks
   - Task 5: Fill documentation gaps (if any)
   - Task 6: First operational task (per role definition)
   
7. [AUTONOMOUS] Emit bootstrap-complete event
   - Audit log: agent_id, scope, context_loaded, gaps_found, first_tasks_completed
   - Transition: BOOTSTRAP → ACTIVE_OPS
```

---

## Cross-Cutting Observations

### Relationship Between Components

```
Symphony (orchestration)
    │
    ├── WATCH: Polls control planes
    │
    ├── BOOTSTRAP: Calls ORBIT → Day-One Bootstrap Skill
    │       │
    │       ├── ORBIT Read: Context Pack API
    │       └── Access provisioning (§11.1)
    │
    ├── EXECUTE: Agent Runtime + Policy Compliance Skill
    │       │
    │       ├── Autonomy Classifier (🟢/🟡/🔴)
    │       ├── Change Manifest Validator
    │       ├── Calibrated Uncertainty Self-Check
    │       └── Audit-Log Emitter (every decision point)
    │
    ├── SUPERVISE: Health monitoring + restart
    │
    ├── CLOSE: Proof-of-work validation
    │       └── Audit-Log Emitter (outcome)
    │
    └── LEARN: ORBIT Write (cumulative learning append)
            └── Audit-Log Emitter (learning event)
```

### Key Design Decisions Observed

1. **Policy-as-code** (WORKFLOW.md) — agent behavior versioned alongside source code
2. **Append-only learning** — ORBIT never overwrites, always enriches
3. **Evidence over confidence** — machine-verifiable evidence required, not confidence language
4. **State transitions as audit points** — emit logs on meaningful transitions, not every tick
5. **Deterministic layer membership** — Inner/Near/Outer classification is rule-based, not ML-predicted
6. **Purpose-limited context packs** — different purposes (BOOTSTRAP vs. EXECUTE) get different budgets

### APIs and Tools Referenced

| System | API Pattern | Purpose |
|--------|-------------|---------|
| ORBIT | `GET /orbit/context?user={}&dimensions={}&layers={}&purpose={}` | Read context packs |
| ORBIT | Append to learning store (write) | Cumulative learning |
| Symphony | WORKFLOW.md (config) + Orchestrator GenServer (runtime) | Lifecycle management |
| Jira | JQL eligibility queries + REST API | Control plane (Watch) |
| JSM/Opsgenie | Alert/incident APIs | Control plane (SRE Watch) |
| Agent Runtime | OpenClaw / Rovo Dev CLI | Agent execution |
| Audit Sink | Event emission (Kafka/StreamHub) | Durable audit trail |
| TWG | Entity resolution + graph queries | Data backbone |

### Gaps and Open Questions

1. **No formal API spec for Symphony callbacks** — The lifecycle is well-described conceptually but no OpenAPI/gRPC contract exists yet in documentation
2. **ORBIT Write API not yet formalized** — Read (Context Pack v1) is well-specified; the write/append path for learning is described conceptually but lacks a concrete API schema
3. **Audit log sink selection** — Multiple patterns exist (StreamHub, Kafka, SQS); the specific durable sink for AI employee audit logs is not yet declared
4. **Policy pack format** — The 🟢/🟡/🔴 model and six rules are well-documented as principles; the machine-readable policy pack format (OPA-style? YAML?) needs specification
5. **Day-One access provisioning** — Identity team dependency for OBO token exchange and agent accounts is flagged as "in-flight" with no firm delivery date[0m
