## 6. Model Card Standard (Mitchell et al. / HuggingFace)

### What it is
The Model Card framework (Mitchell et al., 2019, "Model Cards for Model Reporting") provides a structured documentation format for ML models covering intended use, performance metrics, ethical considerations, and limitations.

### How it works — Standard Sections

Based on the Mitchell et al. framework and as adapted at Atlassian (via enterprise customer questionnaire and internal System Card template):

| Section | Content | ML Deployment Manifest Analog |
|---------|---------|-------------------------------|
| **1. Model Details** | Name, version, developer, family, architecture | `model.name`, `model.version`, `model.architecture` |
| **2. Intended Use** | In-scope use cases, intended users, out-of-scope uses, regions | `intent`, `non_goals` |
| **3. Factors** | Demographic/environmental/instrumentation factors affecting results | `risk.factors` |
| **4. Metrics** | Performance metrics and why chosen | `evaluation.metrics` |
| **5. Evaluation Data** | Datasets used, representativeness | `evaluation.datasets` |
| **6. Training Data** | Data the model was trained on | `lineage.training_data` |
| **7. Quantitative Analyses** | Performance broken down by factors | `evaluation.slice_analysis` |
| **8. Ethical Considerations** | Sensitive data, human safety implications, risk mitigation | `risk.ethical` |
| **9. Caveats & Recommendations** | Known limitations, deployment recommendations | `non_goals`, `risk.known_limitations` |

### Atlassian's Internal "System Card" Template

From internal documentation, Atlassian has adapted model cards into "System Cards" with these sections:

```yaml
system_card:
  system_overview:
    product_name: ""
    usecase_id: ""  # Central AI communication ID
    description: ""
  intended_use:
    users: []
    workflows: []
    non_goals: []  # Explicit "do not use for..."
  ai_capabilities:
    features: []
    models_providers: []
  data_flow:
    inputs: []     # What user/customer data is sent to AI
    exclusions: [] # "no passwords or secrets"
    outputs: []    # What is returned
  performance_limitations:
    optimized_for: []
    known_failures: []  # Hallucinations, bias risks, language limitsred_lines: []       # "do not interpret as compliance/legal advice"
  risks_mitigations:
    key_risks: []       # Privacy, security, fairness, misuse
    guardrails: []      # UX guardrails, rate limits, loggingsecurity_controls: []
  deployment_scope:
    plans: []           # Standard/Premium/Enterprise
    deployment_models: [] # Cloud/Isolated Cloud/AGCconstraints: []
  ownership:
    product_team: ""
    tech_owner: ""
    security_contact: ""
```

### How it applies
The Model Card becomes the **documentation byproduct** section of the deployment manifest. The skill should auto-generate this from existing metadata:

```yaml
model_card:
  intent: "Re-rank search results for content relevance"
  non_goals:
    - "Not intended for content moderation decisions"
    - "Not intended for user profiling or behavioral prediction"
    - "Not for use in FedRAMP High environments without IC validation"
  limitations:
    - "Performance degrades on queries< 3 tokens"
    - "Not trained on non-English content"
  fairness:
    metrics_evaluated: [equalized_odds, demographic_parity_difference]
    slices_tested: [region, tenant_size, language]
  risks:
    - type: data_drift
      detection: "PSI monitor on feature distributions, threshold 0.15"
      mitigation: "Auto-retrain trigger + alert to ML owner"
    - type: latency_regression
      detection: "P99 > 200ms for 5min sustained"
      mitigation: "Auto-rollback to previous model version"
```

**Source**: Mitchell et al. (2019) "Model Cards for Model Reporting" (Google); [Template for System Card](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120204d201f1c903d4480b84c92d16ad3473d/pages/6300644614/); [TRUSTHELP-4365AI Model Card questionnaire](https://hello.jira.atlassian.cloud/browse/TRUSTHELP-4365); [AI fairness & data risks](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~70121eeecde7086e94a778d189b8b5d0a90f2/pages/5749449742/)

