## 8. Pre-Deployment Validation Checklist Pattern

### What it is
The ML Platform defines a structured checklist pattern for validating models before deployment, capturing readiness criteria as gates.

### How it works — Validation Matrix

| Check | Prevents | How |
|-------|----------|-----|
| Package exists in registry | Missing artifacts | Registry API check |
| Package loads correctly | Platform stability issues | Launchpad notebook |
| Model input/output matches spec | User errors from packaging | Schema validation |
| Model compatible with container | Code errors | Container startup test |
| Model compatible with instance | OOM/disk errors | Resource constraint check |
| Safe file format (no pickle/pt/h5) | Security risks | Format gate (COMMIT-27251) |
| Latency within KR | SLO breach | Load test via PerfHammer |
| Prediction quality check | Regression | Batch inference comparison |

### How it applies

```yaml
pre_deployment_validation:
  gates:
    - name: artifact_exists
      check: registry_lookup
      required: true
    - name: format_safety
      check: reject_unsafe_formats# .pkl, .pt, .h5
      required: true
    - name: model_loads
      check: launchpad_startup
      required: true
    - name: schema_validation
      check: input_output_match
      required: true
    - name: latency_check
      check: perfhammer_benchmark
      threshold_p99_ms: 200
      required: true
    - name: quality_regression
      check: batch_inference_comparison
      baseline_ref: "latest_training_baseline"
      min_mrr_delta: -0.02
      required: true
```

**Source**: [Pre-Deployment Checklist](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6186363172/), [How To: Deploy ML Models to TEAMServe](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120204aa07fe7450f489899b60900ad6a0967/pages/5959589965/)

