## 4. TEAMServe Model Deployment Configuration

### What it is
TEAMServe is Atlassian's internal model-as-a-service platform (analogous to SageMaker but on Kubernetes/GKE/EKS + ArgoCD). It uses GitOps-style YAML configurations for model deployments.

### How it works — Application YAML

```yaml
apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1
kind: Application
metadata:
  name: trtllm-serve-gemma-3-4b-it
  annotations:
    modelOwners: '["engineer_id"]'
    serviceConsumers: |
      - serviceId: micros/convo-ai
        regions: [us-west-2, eu-west-1]
        maxLoadPercent: 40
spec:
  source:
    repoURL: <teamserve-repo>
    chart: trtllm-serve  # Helm chart
    helm:
      valuesObject:
        replicas: 1
        region: us-west-2
        environment: prod
        model:
          group: teamserve
          version: gemma-3-4b-it-202510202240
          backend: pytorch
          extraLLMApiOptions: low_latency.yaml
```

### TEAMServe Endpoint Configuration

```yaml
teamserve:
  client:
    baseUrl: <endpoint-url>
    socketTimeout: 800model:
    endpoints:
      - endpointName: l2-rerank-v2
        endpointUrl: /hybrid-reranker-model/versions/deployment-global/v2/models/triton_l2_reranker/infer
```

### Model V2 Configuration Pattern

```yaml
modelV2:
  name: l2-new-lookup
  group: deployment-uswest2-25# ML-registry deployment group alias
  platform: teamserve
  requestType: triton
```

### How it applies
The TEAMServe pattern shows how ML-specific deployment configs should be structured:
- Model version pinning via registry references
- Region-specific endpoint routing
- Consumer authorization declarations
- Rolling update strategy (maxSurge/maxUnavailable for GPU constraints)

**Source**: [TEAMServe documentation](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202025d1dbcaea7d43e298e8ae74fe5dcb9f/pages/5623633161/API+overview), [Current state of model deployment workflows](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020cd3f787132154dc3b533d4df685f7759/pages/5881992883/)

