## 7. ML Registry Deployment Metadata

### What it is
Atlassian's ML Platform tracks model deployments in ML Registry as "Deployment Components" with versioned deployment instances. This provides the metadata schema for what should be captured in a deployment manifest.

### How it works — Registry Entities

| Component | Fields |
|-----------|--------|
| **Model Service** (long-lived) | Owner, cost centre, API endpoint, access controls, deployment history, active config (shadow/canary/progressive), deployment pipeline, repository |
| **Deployment Instance** (ephemeral) | ML Model Artifact, Inference Container Image, Compute Infrastructure Config, Environment Config, API Permissions, Feature Service, Alerting rules |

### Deployment Configuration as Artifacts

Deployment versions capture:
- Manifest config files (Kube deployment YAML)
- Model artifact reference (registry component version)
- Infrastructure configuration (GPU type, replicas, region)
- Alerting/monitoring rules

### How it applies

The deployment manifest should reference and extend registry metadata:

```yaml
registry:
  component_id: "deployment-component-uuid"
  model_version_ref: "model-component-id/version-id"
  lineage_trace: true
deployment_instance:
  model_artifact:
    registry_ref: "l2-ranker.Model/004"
    format: onnx
    safe_format_validated: true  # Per COMMIT-27251
  container:
    image: "docker.atl-paas.net/triton-server:24.01"
    backend: pythoncompute:
    instance_type: g5.2xlarge
    gpu_count: 1
    replicas: 3
  environment:
    region: us-west-2
    cluster: teamserve-prod-uswest2
```

**Source**: [Model Deployments in ML Lifecycle](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6122166900/), [Model Deployments Now in ML Registry & Lineage](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/blog/2026/01/15/6317041646/)

