## Finding 2: ORBIT Internal Data Model — Snapshot and Feature Store Schema

### What it is
ORBIT's internal storage layer that powers the Context Pack API. The data model has two levels: **Orbit Snapshots** (per-user ranked entity views) and **Feature Store entries** (ML signals per user-entity pair).

### How it works

**OrbitSnapshot (internal, per user):**
```plaintext
OrbitSnapshot {
  tenantId
  userId
  snapshotId
  createdAt
  decayEpoch              // used to recompute decayed scores
  entities: [OrbitEntityEntry]
  edges:[OrbitEdgeEntry]
  previousSnapshotId?// for delta computation
  deltaFromPrevious?      // "what changed since..."
}
```

**OrbitEntityEntry (per user-entity pair):**
```plaintext
OrbitEntityEntry {
  entityRef {
    entityId             // TwG ID
    entityType           // PERSON | TEAM | PROJECT | TICKET | DOC | REPO | PULL_REQUEST | INCIDENT | SERVICE}
  orbitScore             // numeric relevance score
  layer                  // INNER | NEAR | OUTER
  reasonCodes[]          // e.g. ROLE_ASSIGNEE, EDITED_RECENTLY, VIEWED_RECENTLY
  evidence[] {
    signalType           // VIEWED_RECENTLY, COMMENTED_RECENTLY, etc.
    timestamp
    relatedEntityRef?
  }
  features? {
    recencyDecay
    frequencyScore
    ownershipStrength
    collaborationIntensity
    urgencyScore
  }
}
```

**Feature Store Schema (Tecton/MLFS):**
```yaml
apiVersion: "v1alpha1"
name: "orbit-schema"
owner: "central-ai-modeling"
columns:
  - name: tenant_id
    type: String
    primary: true
  - name: tenant_id_type
    type: String
    primary: true
  - name: user_aaid
    type: String
    primary: true
  - name: timestamp
    type: Timestamp
```

**OrbitFeatures (per user-entity pair — signal level):**
```plaintext
OrbitFeatures(u, e) {
  // recency
  lastActivityAt
  recencyDecay

  // frequency
  viewCount7d, viewCount30d, editCount30d, commentCount30d
  frequencyScore

  // ownership
  isCreator, isAssignee, isReporter, isDocOwner, isPRAuthor, isPRReviewer
  ownershipStrength

  // collaboration
  numDistinctCollaborators30d, numCommentsByOthers30d
  collaborationIntensity

  // urgency
  dueInDays?, isBlocker?, incidentSeverity?
  urgencyScore

  // explicit controls
  pinnedByUser, hiddenByUser, manualRankOverride?
}
```

### How it applies to the skill

The **ORBIT read skill** at instantiation must:
1. Provide the agent's scope identifier (service ARI, repo ARI, or team ARI)
2. Specify the appropriate `purpose` (`AGENT_PLAN` for planning, `AGENT_EXECUTE` for action)
3. Consume the structured pack with entities, artifacts, edges
4. Parse reason codes to understand WHY each entity is relevant (enables the agent to make informed decisions about which context to prioritize)

### Source
- [ORBIT data model](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202027e1af5d30e94112880666ee62f9277a/pages/6628226631)
- [Orbit engineering](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~29301718/pages/6629525234)
- [ORBIT / Rovo context](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202027e1af5d30e94112880666ee62f9277a/pages/6628129082)

