## 5. Domain-Specific Terminology the AI Must Understand

| Term | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| **Shadow variant** | Receives replicated traffic, responses logged not returned to caller |
| **Production variant** | Active variant serving real user traffic |
| **Canary stack** | New deployment receiving a % of real traffic |
| **Baseline stack** | Same-version deployment provisioned fresh for clean comparison |
| **PDV** | Post-Deployment Verification — checks run before DNS cutover |
| **runOnce** | Micros/Pollinator check triggered once during deployment |
| **Kayenta** | Spinnaker's canary analysis service using SignalFx metrics |
| **Switcheroo** | Atlassian's control plane for feature flag management |
| **Statsig Experiment** | A/B test with auto-attached secondary metrics and SPRT |
| **Feature Gate** | Boolean flag for kill-switch or operational toggles |
| **RolloutService** | Java API for gating code paths behind flags in Jira monolith |
| **Pollinator** | Atlassian's synthetic check platform for PDV |
| **MICROS_SERVICE_DOMAIN_NAME** | DNS alias pointing to canary stack for PDV targeting |
| **Launchpad** | TEAMServe staging environment for pre-deployment validation |
| **Tarot v3** | ML Registry for model artifact management and compliance metadata |
| **ArgoCD** | GitOps sync for TEAMServe deployments |
| **Multi-model packed** | Single endpoint serving multiple model versions (enables in-place canary) |

