## 6. Evaluation Reporting Integration (rovo-eval / AIX-eval)

### 6.1 AIX-eval Reporting Pattern

**What it is**: Atlassian's internal LLM evaluation framework with MLflow integration for metrics reporting.

**Key Reporting Capabilities**:
- Metrics logged to MLflow for experiment tracking
- YAML-based configuration (EVaC — Evaluations as Code)
- Results written to Databricks tables for dashboard creation
- Supports LLM-as-judge metrics + traditional NLP metrics

**Standard Evaluation Report Fields**:
- Metric name, mean score, min, max, std dev
- Per-model comparison tables
- Per-dataset breakdowns
- Judge pass/fail rates

### 6.2 rovo-eval Reporting Pattern

**What it is**: The assistant evaluation service for end-to-end quality metrics on golden datasets.

**Reporting Flow**:
- Upload dataset → trigger evaluation → metrics calculation → dashboard
- Supports online (production traffic) and offline (on-demand) evaluation
- Results stored in Postgres + streamed to Socrates/Statsig

**How it applies to the skill**:
- Evaluation reports from the ML lifecycle should integrate with both frameworks
- AIX-eval for offline model quality assessment
- rovo-eval for production deployment verification
- Reports should include judge scores, regression status, and confidence intervals

**Source**: [SPIKE: ML Evaluation Framework](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202036af61f960604897b3e8da6cda3794c0/pages/6098222361), [AIX-Eval](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120203bd0205883eb4c12af95fe0e997be99f/pages/6522081308)

