## 6. Pattern: Integration with §10.5 Escalation Thresholds

### What it is
The calibration check directly feeds into the Symphony autonomy tier classifier. The §10.5 escalation thresholds define precisely when the agent must stop autonomous operation.

### Escalation trigger conditions (combining confidence + policy)

```yaml
escalation_triggers:
  # Confidence-based triggers
  - condition: "calibrated_confidence < 0.60"
    action: "🔴 ESCALATE"
    reason: "Confidence below escalation floor"
  - condition: "calibrated_confidence < 0.85AND action.risk_class IN [high, restricted]"
    action: "🔴 ESCALATE"  
    reason: "Insufficient confidence for high-risk action"
    
  - condition: "calibrated_confidence BETWEEN 0.60 AND 0.85"
    action: "🟡 CONFIRM"
    reason: "Medium confidence — propose with reasoning"

  # Knowledge-boundary triggers (always escalate regardless of confidence)
  - condition: "evidence_basis == 'assumed' AND action.is_write_operation"
    action: "🔴 ESCALATE"
    reason: "Cannot take write action based on unverified assumption"
    
  - condition: "conflicting_signals > 2"
    action: "🔴 ESCALATE"
    reason: "Multiple conflicting signals — human judgment needed"
    
  - condition: "domain NOT IN agent.bootstrapped_domains"
    action: "🔴 ESCALATE"
    reason: "Operating outside bootstrapped expertise"

  # Action-class blocklist (never autonomous regardless of confidence)
  - condition: "action.class IN restricted_actions"
    action: "🔴 ESCALATE (ALWAYS)"
    reason: "Restricted action class requires human approval"
    restricted_actions:
      - "delete_*"
      - "modify_permissions"
      - "change_billing"
      - "production_config_change"
      - "cross_tenant_operation"
```

### Source
- [Symphony: AI Employee Orchestration Platform](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202027e1af5d30e94112880666ee62f9277a/pages/6933824809): 3-tier autonomy model definition
