## 4. Retention Requirements

### 4.1 Atlassian Internal Standards

| Source | Retention | Notes |
|--------|-----------|-------|
| Atlassian Logging Standard | **365 days minimum** | For audit, access, and security logs |
| Current Admin Hub ALP | 180 days | Being extended to 365 days (ATLAS-105134, at risk) |
| Enterprise target | **365+ days** configurable | Industry standard for regulated customers |
| BOR-1844 (immutable audit) | 90 days | GDPR-compliant, zero-PII |
| RFC-18 (S3 cold) | Indefinite | Cold storage for policy-derive |

### 4.2 External Compliance Requirements

| Framework | Requirement |
|-----------|-------------|
| **EU AI Act Art. 12/19** | Automatic logging of AI system operation; providers must retain logs generated by high-risk AI (A.6.2.8 in ISO 42001) |
| **NIST AI RMF §3.4** | Accountability & Transparency: complete audit trails linking actions to data, policies, and reasoning |
| **NIST 800-53AU-2** | Define events to log; retain per compliance schedule |
| **SOC 2** | Complete, tamper-evident, attributable audit trail |
| **ISO 42001 A.6.2.8** | Event log recording must be enabled when AI is in use |

### 4.3 Recommendation for Symphony

- **Hot path (Splunk/ALP):** 365 days — queryable for investigations and compliance
- **Cold path (S3/Parquet):** 7 years — aligned with financial/regulatory long-term retention
- **Reasoning traces:** 90 days hot, 2 years cold (larger payloads, less frequent query)

