## 5. Required Emission Points Across Symphony Skills

The audit-log emitter tool must be invoked at specific lifecycle points by each skill in the Symphony governance stack:

### 5.1Emission Point Matrix

| Skill | Emission Points | Event Types |
|-------|----------------|-------------|
| **Symphony Orchestrator (Watch→Close→Learn)** | Work item detected; Agent spawned; Agent health check; Work item closed; ORBIT enriched | `detected:work-item`, `bootstrapped:agent`, `restarted:agent`, `completed:work-item`, `enriched:orbit-context` |
| **ORBIT Read/Write** | Context bootstrap at instantiation; Learning append on task completion | `bootstrapped:agent` (with context-pack metadata), `enriched:orbit-context` |
| **Policy Compliance + Autonomy Classifier** | Every autonomy-tier decision; Every change manifest validation; Every escalation | `executed:action` (🟢), `requested:confirmation` (🟡), `escalated:decision` (🔴), `validated:change-manifest`, `violated:policy` |
| **Calibrated-Uncertainty Self-Check** | Every confidence assessment that affects tier classification; Every "I don't know" decision | Embedded in the evidence block: `confidenceLevel`, `confidenceType` (measured vs inferred), `uncertaintyFlag` |
| **Day-One Bootstrap** | Access provisioned; Documents ingested; First tasks assigned | `bootstrapped:agent` (with access grants), `enriched:orbit-context` (document ingest), `detected:work-item` (first tasks) |

### 5.2 Mandatory vs. Optional Fields Per Emission Point

**Always required (every emission):**
- `actor.id` (agent ARI)
- `actor.onBehalfOf` (service owner)
- `time` (ISO-8601)
- `correlationId` (work item or session)
- `container` (org scope)
- `policyRef` (which policy version governs)
- `autonomyTier` (🟢/🟡/🔴)

**Required for action events:**
- Full intent block (description, non-goals, invariants)
- Full evidence block (signal source, observed value, confidence)
- Approval block (required/obtained/mechanism)
- Outcome block (status, result summary, blast radius)

**Required for change manifest validation:**
- Intent + non-goals + invariants + risk classification
- Test plan reference
- Rollback plan reference
- Post-deploy monitoring plan

