## 7. rovo-eval & AIX-eval

### Internal Wrappers Discovered

**AIX-eval** (`atlassian-ai-experience-evaluation` package, aka `aixeval`)
- **What it is**: Python-based offline evaluation framework for LLM features
- **How it works**:
  - Modes: **Evaluate** (metrics on pre-existing outputs), **Generate** (produce LLM responses)
  - Environments: local terminal, Databricks notebooks, ML Studio
  - Latest: **EVaC** (Evaluations as Code) — YAML config +2 lines of Python
  - Integrates with AI Gateway for model access- Logs results to MLflow for experiment tracking
  - Metrics: LLM-as-judge + traditional NLP metrics
- **ML Studio module**: `aixeval_run` — runs as standard ML Studio module
- **Source**: [AIX-Eval](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120203bd0205883eb4c12af95fe0e997be99f/pages/6522081308)

**Rovo-eval (Assistant Evaluation Service)**
- **What it is**: Production evaluation service for e2e agent/assistant quality
- **How it works**:
  - Portal: `go/rovoeval`
  - Calls agents in convo-ai, calculates end-to-end quality metrics on golden datasets
  - Supports multi-turn conversations, feature flags for A/B testing
  - Experiment cloning, dashboards, scheduling
  - Used for: Rovo Chat, SAIN, Reading Aids, CSM, OOTB agents
- **Source**: [SPIKE: ML Evaluation Framework](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202036af61f960604897b3e8da6cda3794c0/pages/6098222361)

**Comparison Matrix**:
| Requirement | Rovo-eval | AIX-eval |
|-------------|-----------|----------|
| ConvoAI Integration | Excellent (Built-in) | Good (Custom) |
| ML Studio Integration | Poor (Centralized) | Excellent (Native) |
| User Simulation | Good (Multi-turn) | Limited |
| Prompt Tuning | Fair (Manual A/B) | Excellent (Systematic) |
| Metrics Calculations | Limited (Kotlin) | Excellent (Python) |
| Data Access | Limited (Uploaded) | Excellent (Production data) |

