## 1. MLflow Tracking & Experiment Logging

### Internal Wrappers Discovered

**`atlassian_ml_studio_sdk.ml_flow` package**
- **What it is**: Platform-provided MLflow setup/tracking SDK used inside ML Studio modules
- **How it works**: Provides `setup_mlflow()` wrapper that configures tracking URI, experiment path, and run context automatically. Pattern: `mlflow.set_tracking_uri("databricks://socrates-public:ml-databricks")` → `mlflow.set_experiment("/Workspace/Shared/...")` → `mlflow.start_run()`
- **Key patterns observed**:
  - Run naming: `Model_<TS>` convention (e.g., `"my_model_v2_retrain_001"`)
  - Flattened params via `mlflow.log_param()`
  - Per-segment metrics via `mlflow.log_metric()`
  - Nested runs for parent workflow + child module tracking
  - Default experiment naming: `/Users/<current_user>/coreml-<table_name>-<date>`
- **Source**: [MLflow Integration in Airlock Flows](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/xugc/pages/6659921772), [M4Critical Workflow Capabilities](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/PPDL/pages/6806432498)

**MLflow Usage in ML Studio (quantified)**:
| Function | Usage Count |
|----------|-------------|
| `log_param` | 235 |
| `log_metric` | 167 |
| `start_run` | 116 |
| `log_artifact` | 104 |
| `artifacts.download_artifacts` | 79 |
| `set_experiment` | 39 |
| `set_tag` | 36 |
| `register_model` | 1 |

**`mlexp` CLI** (Repo: `model-eval-tool/mlexp/`)
- **What it is**: Lightweight file-backed experiment tracking CLI for L2 ranker research
- **How it works**: State in `~/.mlexp/experiments.jsonl`. Commands:
  - `mlexp log --yaml<workflow.yaml> --blueprint-id <id>` — log a run with YAML params
  - `mlexp track --latest --auto-sync` — poll live run, sync metrics
  - `mlexp sync-l2 <run-id>` — pull MRR@10000/NDCG from Databricks output tables
  - `mlexp diff <id1> <id2>` — side-by-side comparison
  - `mlexp fetch-mlflow <run-id>` — bridge MLS run IDs to MLflow training metrics
  - `mlexp watch <run-id>` — overnight daemon with auto-fix
- **How it applies**: This is a reusable pattern for bridging ML Studio orchestration with MLflow metrics tracking
- **Source**: [L2 Autoresearch Harness](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/rdm/pages/6975061989)

**`msr_model_registering` package** (part of `atlassian-cml-msr-sdk`)
- **What it is**: MSR SDK module providing MLflow integration for model versioning, tracking, and artifact management
- **How it works**: Install via `poetry add atlassian-cml-msr-sdk`, provides wrapper for experiment tracking + model registry operations
- **Source**: [Getting Started with Core ML MSR SDK](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DTIE/pages/5120491165)

**`msp_register_mlflow`** (ML Studio module)
- **What it is**: The MLflow → Tarot bridge module — accounts for majority of model bytes entering Tarot
- **How it works**: Downloads model artifact from MLflow, repackages, uploads to Tarot v3 registry with compliance metadata
- **Source**: [ML Studio Workflow Opportunities](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020f42e6ad0a6ee44319b956587ec99b127/pages/6974941522)

