- **Source**: [MLFS SDK adoption guide](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6721137225)

**MLFS Python DSL** (for Batch Feature View definitions)
- **What it is**: Python SDK for defining features as code (purpose-built for Atlassian ecosystem)
- **How it works**: Similar to Tecton SDK but with native support for:
  - Atlassian data source types (ML Studio tables, GasV3 tables)
  - ASAP/Slauth auth (no Tecton API keys)
  - Compliance with data governance policies out-of-box
- **Source**: [MLFS Batch Feature View MVP blog](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/blog/2026/02/18/6490265832)

**Tecton SDK patterns** (being deprecated by Nov 2026):
```python
from tecton import batch_feature_view, Entity, Aggregation
@batch_feature_view(
    sources=[source], entities=[user], mode="batch",
    aggregations=[Aggregation(column="score", function="avg", time_window="1d")],
    ttl="30d"
)
def user_features(df): return df[["id", "score", "created_at"]]
```

**Migration Pattern**: Feature flag gating between Tecton and MLFS reads, shadow testing, then cutover
- **Source**: [Tecton to MLFS Migration Roadmap](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6068686994)

