# Research Findings: Symphony Governance + Day-One Bootstrap Stack (Cluster H, Items i–n)

## Executive Summary

This research investigates the Symphony/ORBIT/Policy governance layer and Day-One bootstrap capabilities for AI employees at Atlassian. The findings are drawn from authoritative internal documentation: the [AI Employee Strategy](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202027e1af5d30e94112880666ee62f9277a/pages/6742955831/AI+Employee+Strategy), [Atlassian Symphony: AI Employee Orchestration Platform](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202027e1af5d30e94112880666ee62f9277a/pages/6933824809), [Agentic Operations in the New SDLC](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202027e1af5d30e94112880666ee62f9277a/pages/6885869718), [ORBIT Personalization & Context Packaging Layer](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202049b56fb3ef7b49abbbe4f53dbbf12160/pages/6272801311), [Policy for AI Agents in SDLC](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~cknott/pages/6676494313), [Autonomous Approval Verification System](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~cknott/pages/6676398058), and [Audit Logs Platform FY26+ Charter](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/aul/pages/5619059552).

---

## (i) Symphony Orchestrator Interface Skill — Watch→Bootstrap→Execute→Supervise→Close→Learn Lifecycle

### What It Is
The Symphony orchestration loop is Atlassian's canonical6-stage lifecycle for AI employee fleet management. It turns work surfaces (Jira, JSM, ML pipelines) into a continuous control plane.

### How It Works (Concrete Steps per Stage)

| Stage | Action | Inputs | Outputs | Human Role |
|-------|--------|--------|---------|------------|
| **Watch** | Continuously polls control planes (JSM, Jira boards, ML experiment queues) for new work items | Control plane APIs, JQL watchers, webhook triggers | New work item detected event | Sets scope and policy; Symphony handles watching |
| **Bootstrap** | Spawns dedicated AI employee agent; ORBIT loads context pack scoped to the task | Work item ID, role type, scope assignment | Running agent instance with hydrated context | No action needed — automatic |
| **Execute** | Agent runs within policy-scoped workspace; takes autonomous actions for🟢 patterns; escalates for 🟡/🔴 | Context pack, policy set, available tools/skills | Reasoning traces, intermediate artifacts, escalation requests | Approves 🟡actions; decides🔴 escalations |
| **Supervise** | Monitors agent health; restarts stalled/crashed agents; preserves work item ownership across restarts | Agent heartbeat, execution progress, timeout thresholds | Health status, restart events | Receives escalations at policy boundaries |
| **Close** | Agent delivers output; reasoning trace captured for review | Completed work artifact, reasoning trace | Resolved incident/merged PR/validated result + audit record | Reviews outcomes, not status updates |
| **Learn** | Each completed work item enriches ORBIT context layer for that service/repo/model | Execution summary, outcome quality signal, causal graph | Updated ORBIT signals, encoded lessons, Spec constraints | None — continuous improvement loop |

### How It Applies (Skill Encoding)

**Justification for new skill**: No existing tool encodes this lifecycle as a step-by-step orchestration workflow the agent itself follows. The existing Symphony platform is infrastructure-level — what's missing is the **agent-side interface skill** that tells the AI employee *how* to participate in each stage (report readiness, accept bootstrap context, signal stage transitions, emit health heartbeats, trigger learning append).

**Skill structure (SKILL.md)**:
```
## Workflow: Symphony Lifecycle Participation
### Stage: WATCH_ACKNOWLEDGMENT
- Accept work item assignment from Symphony dispatcher
- Validate work item matches role scope
- Confirm readiness to bootstrap

### Stage: BOOTSTRAP_INGESTION
- Request ORBIT context pack (purpose: AGENT_EXECUTE)
- Ingest service spec, incident history, runbooks, observability config
- Confirm bootstrap complete → signal READY

### Stage: EXECUTE
- For each action: classify autonomy tier (🟢/🟡/🔴)
- Execute 🟢 autonomously; propose 🟡 with reasoning; escalate 🔴 with full context
- Emit reasoning trace per action
- Emit heartbeat every N seconds

### Stage: SUPERVISE_COMPLIANCE
- Respond to health checks
- Report stall conditions proactively
- Preserve state for restart continuity

### Stage: CLOSE
- Package deliverables (artifact + reasoning trace + outcome assessment)
- Signal CLOSE to Symphony orchestrator
- Await human review acknowledgment

### Stage: LEARN
- Summarize execution (successes, failures, novel patterns discovered)
- Append learning to ORBIT via learning_append API
- Propose policy updates if gaps identified
```

**Source**: [Atlassian Symphony: AI Employee Orchestration Platform](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202027e1af5d30e94112880666ee62f9277a/pages/6933824809) + [AI Employee Strategy](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202027e1af5d30e94112880666ee62f9277a/pages/6742955831)

