## Gap Analysis: Existing Tools vs. Required New Artifacts

### What Already Exists (Subtask-1Association Map)

| Existing Capability | Where It Lives | What It Does |
|---|---|---|
| ORBIT Context Pack read API | ORBIT Platform Service (in delivery) | Returns ranked entities for a user/purpose |
| MCP Audit Log (tool invocations) | MCP Server → StreamHub | Logs tool calls with actor/tool/product metadata |
| 3-Tier Autonomy Model (design) | Policy documents, hire_a_tpm kit | Manual tagging of operations as 🟢/🟡/🔴 |
| Change Manifest spec (design) | Autonomous Approval Verification System page | Defines required fields but not an executable validator |
| Confidence scoring (experimental) | CMA S2C Agent experiments | Tests calibration but not an agent-facing skill |
| Symphony lifecycle (architecture) | Symphony platform documentation | Defines the6stages but not agent-side participation protocol |
| Hire via URL (prototype) | AI Lab One-Click SRE | Demonstrates user journey; not encoded as repeatable skill |
| OpenClaw/Rovo Dev runtime | Agent runtime infrastructure | Executes agents; doesn't encode governance workflows |

### What's Missing (Justification for Each New Artifact)

| Item | Type | Gap | Justification |
|------|------|-----|---------------|
| **(i) Symphony Orchestrator Interface** | SKILL | No agent-side protocol for participating in the 6-stage lifecycle | Agents need step-by-step instructions for stage transitions, heartbeats, restart resilience, and learning triggers |
| **(j) ORBIT Read/Write** | SKILL | Read API exists but no skill wraps it for bootstrap + no write/append API for learning | Agents need a skill that knows *when* and *how* to request context packs and append learnings |
| **(k) Policy Compliance + Autonomy Classifier** | SKILL | Policy rules exist as documents; no executable classifier at the agent level | Every action needs programmatic tier classification before execution; manifests need automated validation |
| **(l) Calibrated Uncertainty Self-Check** | SKILL | "Evidence over confidence" is a principle; no enforcement mechanism | Agents need a mandatory self-check workflow that separates measured/inferred/unknown |
| **(m) Audit-Log Emitter** | TOOL | MCP audit logs tool invocations; doesn't log intent/evidence/approval/outcome semantics | Governance requires richer audit events than "tool X was called by user Y" |
| **(n) Day-One Bootstrap** | SKILL | Hire flow exists as prototype; not encoded as repeatable, auditable orchestration | New AI employees need a deterministic onboarding workflow with access → ingest → validate → report |

---

## Cross-Cutting Design Patterns

### Human Confirmation Points

| Artifact | Autonomous (no human) | Requires Confirmation | Always Human |
|----------|----------------------|----------------------|--------------|
| Symphony lifecycle transitions | Stage transitions within Execute | Re-assignment to new scope | Policy updates |
| ORBIT read | Always autonomous | — | — |
| ORBIT write (learning append) | Standard learning | Novel pattern encoding | Policy-changing lessons |
| Autonomy classification | 🟢 classification | — | — |
| Change manifest validation | Structural validation | — | Intent approval |
| Uncertainty self-check | Self-assessment | — | — |
| Audit-log emit | Always autonomous | — | — |
| Day-One bootstrap | Steps3-4 (ingest + self-test) | Step 5 (readiness report) | Step 2 (access provisioning approval) |

### Domain Terminology the AI Must Understand

- **ORBIT layers**: Inner (active working set) / Near (related context) / Outer (background awareness)
- **Context Pack purposes**: HOME_WORKSPACE_RENDER, SEARCH_QUERY_GROUNDING, CHAT_TURN_GROUNDING, AGENT_PLAN, AGENT_EXECUTE
- **Autonomy tiers**: 🟢 Autonomous / 🟡 Confirm / 🔴 Escalate
- **Symphony stages**: Watch / Bootstrap / Execute / Supervise / Close / Learn
- **Reasoning Trace**: Full chain of decisions + evidence leading to an action
- **Permanent Remediation PR**: Code change that prevents a failure class from recurring + encodes lesson into Spec
- **Causal Graph**: Visual map of how a failure cascaded through services
- **Intent Map**: Live graph linking features to telemetry contracts and SLOs
- **Policy Pack**: Versioned set of machine-executable rules governing agent behavior for a role+scope
- **Time-to-Delegation**: North star metric — how quickly a team trusts their AI employee to handle a task autonomously

### Sequencing Dependencies

```
(n) Day-One Bootstrap
  └── requires (j) ORBIT Read (for context pack at bootstrap)
  └── requires (k) Policy Compliance (for classifying first tasks)
  └── requires (m) Audit-Log Emitter (for recording bootstrap actions)
  └── requires (l) Uncertainty Self-Check (for readiness assessment)
  └── invokes (i) Symphony Interface (for signaling READY)

(i) Symphony Interface
  └── invokes (j) ORBIT Read (at Bootstrap stage)
  └── invokes (j) ORBIT Write (at Learn stage)
  └── invokes (m) Audit-Log Emitter (at Close stage)
  └── invokes (k) Policy Compliance (at Execute stage)

(k) Policy Compliance
  └── invokes (l) Uncertainty Self-Check (when classifying novel patterns)
  └── invokes (m) Audit-Log Emitter (when escalating)
```

