## Original User Request
**Description**: Create the ML Lifecycle Execution Stack — skills and tools the AI MLE needs to design experiments, train, evaluate, package, register, deploy, document, and cost-manage models. This covers Clusters B (Training/Experimentation/Evaluation), C (Feature Engineering & Data Quality), D (Packaging/Registry/Deployment/Rollout), F (Cost/Capacity), and G (Stakeholder Communication & Documentation Byproducts). Shared infra justification: all these tools sit on top of MLflow / ML Studio / Databricks SDKs, ML Registry (Tarot v3) client, Tecton/MLFS client, Bitbucket Pipelines/Spinnaker/Micros descriptors, and shared report-generation templates — so they can be designed cohesively. Specific candidates: (a) Training/HPO runner skill+tool wrapping ML Studio/Databricks + Optimus Prime to statistical convergence; (b) MLflow run construction tool enforcing `Model_<TS>` pattern, flattened params, per-segment metrics; (c) Evaluation runner tool(s) for rovo-eval + AIX-eval + multi-seed/k-fold/slice/calibration/fairness reporter; (d) Error-analysis taxonomy skill (data quality / model limitation / feature gap / label noise / distribution shift); (e) Ablation matrix executor tool; (f) Feature lifecycle tool (define→write→hydrate→log→join) for Tecton/MLFS with online/offline consistency check; (g) Proactive data-quality audit skill+tool (coverage/sparsity/freshness by connector/region/tenant); (h) Model packaging via MSP SDK + Tarot v3 registration tool with full compliance metadata; (i) Deployment manifest generator skill (intent+non-goals+invariants+risk+test+rollback+monitoring); (j) Canary/shadow rollout controller for TEAMServe/Triton/SageMaker with feature-flag gating + post-deploy invariant verifier; (k) Architecture comparison report, model card, experiment report, weekly digest, PIR auto-drafter skills+templates; (l) Cost/utilization analyzer tool (FinOps + ML Artifact Cost Monitoring) and SageMaker→TEAMServe migration calculator. Each new tool MUST justify why existing tools (per Subtask 1's Association Map) are insufficient. Reference §2.2-§2.6, §2.8-§2.10, §3.1-§3.2, §4.1 (templates), §4.2, §4.3 (MLflow + Feature Store + cost queries), §4.4 (all templates), §5.1-§5.2, §6.1 (SOP-1) and §6.2 (SOP-2), §11.3 first tasks 1-4 of the role document.

**Todos**:
- Research available APIs/SDKs/CLIs for ML Studio, Databricks, MLflow, Tarot v3, Tecton, MLFS, MSP SDK, TEAMServe, SageMaker, Spinnaker, Micros, Bitbucket Pipelines, FinOps dashboards, Optimus Prime
- Enumerate each new skill/tool with name, purpose, autonomy tier fit, and justification vs. Subtask 1's discovered tools
- Specify the training+HPO+evaluation skill+tool family (SOP-1 / SOP-2 backbone) — multi-seed, k-fold, slice-aware, ablation, calibration, fairness, CIs — enforcing §10.2 'always the proper solution'
- Specify the feature lifecycle + proactive data-quality audit skill+tool (§2.4, §6.2 step 4, §11.3 task 4)
- Specify packaging, Tarot v3 registration, deployment manifest, canary/shadow rollout, post-deploy invariant verifier (§2.5, §2.6, §6.1 deploy phase)
- Specify documentation-byproduct generators: model card, experiment report, architecture comparison report, weekly digest, PIR auto-drafter (§4.4, §7.3)
- Specify cost/capacity analyzer + SageMaker→TEAMServe migration calculator (§2.10, §5.3 migration exemplar)
- For each new skill, list which existing tools (from Subtask 1) it leverages and any additional new tools needed
- Group deliverables into shippable Create subtask packages, mapping each to a §2 responsibility priority
</UserRequest>

